const DBD = {"killers":[{"id":"theanimatronic","name":"The Animatronic","bio":"The Animatronic always comes back.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHelp Wanted\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003ePhantom Fear\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHaywire\u003c/b\u003e, help him compromise generators, make Survivors scream, and regress exit gate switches.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/02/K40_TheAnimatronic_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Haywire","description":"Exit Gate Switches with at least \u003cb\u003e80\u003c/b\u003e% progress regress at \u003cb\u003e80/90/100\u003c/b\u003e% speed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile they are regressing, Survivors see the Exit Gate Lights flicker randomly.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/ff/IconPerks_haywire.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Help Wanted","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, it is compromised.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen that Generator is completed by Survivors, your basic-attack cooldowns are \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% shorter for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOnly 1 Generator can be compromised at a time.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e9/IconPerks_helpWanted.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Phantom Fear","description":"Whenever a Survivor within your Terror Radius looks at you, they scream, then you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e80/70/60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c6/IconPerks_phantomFear.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Fazbear\u0027s Fright","description":"The Animatronic lived to kill, even when his mechanical costume became his tomb.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: FIRE AXE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Animatronic is armed with a \u003cb\u003eFire Axe\u003c/b\u003e that he can throw at Survivors. If the \u003cb\u003eFire Axe\u003c/b\u003e hits a Survivor, the weapon becomes embedded in them, afflicting them with \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e \u0026 \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e until it is removed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL MAP FEATURE: SECURITY SYSTEM\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAt the start of the trial, \u003cb\u003e7 Security Doors\u003c/b\u003e are spawned randomly throughout the map. These \u003cb\u003eDoors\u003c/b\u003e can be accessed by both Survivors and The Animatronic.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEach \u003cb\u003eSecurity Door\u003c/b\u003e has a \u003cb\u003eCamera\u003c/b\u003e attached to it. Interacting with the \u003cb\u003eDoor\u003c/b\u003e gives the Survivor access to the \u003cb\u003eCamera View\u003c/b\u003e, allowing the Survivor to cycle through every \u003cb\u003eCamera\u003c/b\u003e in the map, travel to the \u003cb\u003eDoor\u003c/b\u003e they are currently looking through, and potentially reveal The Animatronic\u0027s aura to the team.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUsing the \u003cb\u003eCameras\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eDoors\u003c/b\u003e too often will deplete the limited battery power available, forcing Survivors to wait until the system reboots. The Animatronic may travel between \u003cb\u003eSecurity Doors\u003c/b\u003e with or without battery power.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf The Animatronic enters a \u003cb\u003eSecurity Door\u003c/b\u003e, they may choose to exit from any other \u003cb\u003eDoor\u003c/b\u003e in the map. Moving to a \u003cb\u003eDoor\u003c/b\u003e already in use by a Survivor will cause The Animatronic to grab that Survivor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUpon entering a Security Door, The Animatronic gains the \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e status effect. The effect lasts 20 seconds after exiting a Security Door, or until revealed by a Survivor on a Security Cam","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/84/IconPowers_fazbearsFright.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theartist","name":"The Artist","bio":"A ranged-reconnaissance Killer, able to launch Dire Crows across the map to reveal and attack Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eGrim Embrace\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eScourge Hook: Pain Resonance\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHex: Pentimento\u003c/b\u003e allow her to interrupt Survivor objectives, torment hooked Survivors, and use destroyed Totems to her advantage.  ","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/01/K26_TheArtist_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Grim Embrace","description":"Whenever you Hook a Survivor for the first time, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you move \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em away from the hooked Survivor, all Generators are blocked for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you have \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, when you move \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em away from the hooked Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAll Generators are blocked for \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Obsession\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1c/IconPerks_grimEmbrace.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/38/PerkAnimation_GrimEmbrace.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hex: Pentimento","description":"You see the Auras of cleansed Totems, and can rekindle each once.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em, Survivors see the Auras of Rekindled Totems.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile a Totem is rekindled, Survivors heal and repair \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% slower, plus \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003e% for each additional Rekindled Totem.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e Totems are rekindled at once, they are blocked.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5d/IconPerks_hexPentimento.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bb/PerkAnimation_HexPentimento_CleansingTotem.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Scourge Hook: Pain Resonance","description":"When the trial starts:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e4 random Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou earn \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e Tokens.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe first time each Survivor is hooked on a Scourge Hook, spend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, then the Generator with the most progress:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eExplodes, loses \u003cb\u003e10/15/20\u003c/b\u003e% progress and starts regressing.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors repairing it scream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/79/IconPerks_scourgeHookPainResonance.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/38/PerkAnimation_ScourgeHookPainResonance.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Birds of Torment","description":"From a wellspring of eternal agony comes a swarm of darkness, a wild and ferocious murder of ink black crows.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge \u003cb\u003eBirds of Torment\u003c/b\u003e. Once fully charged, tap the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to summon a Dire Crow. You can repeat the action quickly by continuously holding down the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e and tapping the \u003ci\u003eAttack Button\u003c/i\u003e again.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen at least one Dire Crow is summoned, it stays idle for a limited time. Spawning a new Dire Crow will extend the time the previously spawned Dire Crow stays idle.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTap the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e to propel the Dire Crows into flight.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDire Crows can inflict damage for a short distance when flying. This is indicated to the Killer by the Dire Crow\u0027s Flight Path.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOnce a Dire Crow continues past the Flight Path, it will no longer inflict damage but can now pass through any obstacles and reveal nearby Survivors using Killer Instinct.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn this phase, Dire Crows will create a swarm around Survivors they hit, allowing the Killer to see the swarm\u0027s aura on the Survivor. The Survivor can repel the swarm by completing the Repel action or entering a locker. During this time, the swarm\u0027s aura is not shown to the Killer.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA Survivor being swarmed will receive damage if hit by a second Dire Crow.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/63/IconPowers_birdsOfTorment.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theblight","name":"The Blight","bio":"An unpredictable Killer, able to rush forward in a burst of speed and carom off obstacles to injure Survivors using his power, \u003cb\u003eBlighted Corruption\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDragon\u0027s Grip\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Undying\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHex: Blood Favor\u003c/b\u003e allow him to impose powerful effects on generators, Totems, and pallets. ","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1f/K21_TheBlight_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dragon’s Grip","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, for the next \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es, the first Survivor that repairs that Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey scream, then you are alerted to their position for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/45/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/ff/IconPerks_dragonsGrip.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Blood Favor","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you damage a Survivor, Upright Pallets within \u003cb\u003e24/28/32\u003c/b\u003em of them are blocked for \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Hex: Undying","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen another Hex Totem is blessed or cleansed, it replaces this one and keeps any Tokens it had.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see the Auras of Survivors within \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003em of Dull Totems.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fe/IconPerks_hexUndying.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Blighted Corruption","description":"Pustula serum courses through his veins, corrupting his mind and body, yet granting him unnatural physical abilities.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: RUSH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to quickly \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e forward. Doing so consumes a \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e token. While performing \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e, The Blight cannot launch an attack.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e into a wall or obstacle in the environment to \u003cb\u003eSlam\u003c/b\u003e onto it. If the \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e fails to connect with a wall or obstacle, or if The Blight is out of \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e tokens, he will enter a short fatigue state and begin recharging the tokens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: LETHAL RUSH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFollowing a \u003cb\u003eSlam\u003c/b\u003e, press the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to launch a \u003cb\u003eLethal Rush\u003c/b\u003e. Doing so consumes a \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e token. A \u003cb\u003eLethal Rush\u003c/b\u003e behaves the same as a \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e, except that The Blight may launch an attack by pressing the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBreaking a dropped pallet consumes up to 2 \u003cb\u003eRush\u003c/b\u003e tokens.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fe/IconPowers_blightedCorruption.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thecannibal","name":"The Cannibal","bio":"A chainsaw-wielding Killer, able to trigger a deadly frenzy using \u003cb\u003eBubba\u0027s Chainsaw\u003c/b\u003e, immediately downing anyone in its path.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eKnock Out\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBarbecue \u0026 Chili\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eFranklin\u0027s Demise\u003c/b\u003e, make Survivors easier to locate while robbing them of their tools and abilities.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6f/K09_TheCannibal_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Barbecue \u0026 Chili","description":"Whenever you hook a Survivor, for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es, you see the Auras of all Survivors who are at least \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003em away from the hooked Survivor.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/51/IconPerks_barbecueAndChilli.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/40/PerkAnimation_BBQ.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Franklin\u0027s Demise","description":"Whenever you damage a Survivor with a basic-attack, they drop their item.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e32/48/64\u003c/b\u003em, you see the Auras of dropped items.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b2/IconPerks_franklinsDemise.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/de/FranklinsDemise_SurvivorPOV.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Knock Out","description":"Whenever a Survivor drops a Pallet, for the next \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003es, if they move \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003em away from it, they gain \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/52/IconPerks_knockOut.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Bubba\u0027s Chainsaw","description":"The Cannibal starts the trial with 3 charges. Press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to consume one charge and perform a \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sweep\u003c/b\u003e attack that can hit multiple targets. Survivors hit during a \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sweep\u003c/b\u003e are put into the dying state. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUse a charge to extend the length of the \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sweep\u003c/b\u003e. Doing this incurs a slightly longer cooldown. Chainsaw charges replenish when the chainsaw is not in use.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe \u003cb\u003eTantrum Meter\u003c/b\u003e slowly fills when revving the Chainsaw. Once the meter is full, or after hitting an object during a \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sweep\u003c/b\u003e, The Cannibal unleashes a \u003cb\u003eTantrum\u003c/b\u003e. The \u003cb\u003eTantrum\u003c/b\u003e damages any Survivor’s around him and puts them into the dying state.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe \u003cb\u003eTantrum\u003c/b\u003e duration increases for each charge that had been used during the \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sweep\u003c/b\u003e. Any remaining charges are lost. During a \u003cb\u003eTantrum\u003c/b\u003e, movement speed is decreased.The \u003cb\u003eTantrum Meter\u003c/b\u003e decreases when the Chainsaw is not in use and completely depletes during a \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sweep\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/79/IconPowers_bubbasChainsaw.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thecenobite","name":"The Cenobite","bio":"A summoning Killer, able to possess chain projectiles and use the Lament Configuration to torture every Survivor at once.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDeadlock\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Plaything\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eScourge Hook: Gift of Pain\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to slow generator progress and continue to torment Survivors who have experienced his sweet suffering.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/K25_TheCenobite_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Deadlock","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, the Generator with the most progress is blocked for \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d3/IconPerks_deadlock.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/50/PerkAnimation_Deadlock.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hex: Plaything","description":"The first time you hook each Survivor, they are hexed and a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003es, the Hex Totem is blocked to other Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe hexed Survivors:\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e24/20/16\u003c/b\u003em of the Hex Totem, they see its Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/18/IconPerks_hexPlaything.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Scourge Hook: Gift of Pain","description":"When the trial starts, 4 random Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor is unhooked from a Scourge Hook:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eHemorrhage\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eMangled\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhen they are healed, until they take damage, they heal and repair \u003cb\u003e10/13/16\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/26/IconPerks_scourgeHookGiftOfPain.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Summons of Pain","description":"An extradimensional gateway that leads to pleasure and pain so great it will tear your soul apart.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to create a gateway and release the button to open it. Once opened, tap the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e to summon forth a possessed chain under your control. Direct the chain into a Survivor to bind them.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA Survivor bound to a chain is unable to sprint. Their movement speed will decrease further as they’re hit with a second and third chain. Survivors can perform the Break Free action to escape.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eLament Configuration:\u003c/b\u003e If left alone, the Lament Configuration initiates a Chain Hunt by summoning chains to pursue Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA Survivor carrying the Lament Configuration will be afflicted with the Oblivious status effect and chains will occasionally be summoned to attack them. The Survivor must solve the Lament Configuration to end the Chain Hunt and remove the puzzle box from their possession. While doing this, The Cenobite will see their location and be able to teleport to it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen The Cenobite picks up the Lament Configuration, a Chain Hunt is activated. Additionally, all Survivors are instantly bound by chains, causing them to scream and reveal their locations.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Lament Configuration will spawn in a new location after The Cenobite or a Survivor has used it.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4d/IconPowers_summonsOfPain.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theclown","name":"The Clown","bio":"A strategic Killer, able to control and corral Survivors by throwing bottles of \u003cb\u003eThe Afterpiece Tonic\u003c/b\u003e to create clouds of noxious gas that cover large areas for a short amount of time. Survivors Intoxicated by the gas are inflicted with impaired vision and movement speed, and give away their location by coughing loudly.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBamboozle\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCoulrophobia\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003ePop Goes the Weasel\u003c/b\u003e, provide vaulting advantages and negatively impact Survivor healing speed and repairs.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d1/K12_TheClown_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Bamboozle","description":"Whenever you vault a Window, it is blocked for Survivors for \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou basic-vault Windows \u003cb\u003e5/10/15\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOnly 1 Window can be blocked at a time.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7a/IconPerks_bamboozle.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Coulrophobia","description":"Survivors within your Terror Radius:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eHeal \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhile healing, basic Skill Checks spin \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/45/IconPerks_coulrophobia.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Pop Goes the Weasel","description":"Whenever you hook a Survivor, for the next \u003cb\u003e35/40/45\u003c/b\u003es, when you damage a Generator, it explodes and loses \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0f/IconPerks_popGoesTheWeasel.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"The Afterpiece Tonic","description":"Throughout his years experimenting with anesthetics and muscle relaxants, The Clown developed several effective concoctions and formulas. He has used his favorite, The Afterpiece Tonic, to great effect, intoxicating and capturing many unwilling victims. The associated Afterpiece Antidote also has useful effects.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTap the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to switch between the \u003cb\u003eAfterpiece Tonic\u003c/b\u003e and the \u003cb\u003eAfterpiece Antidote\u003c/b\u003e. Tap or hold and release the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to launch a bottle.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to replenish your bottles.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Afterpiece Tonic\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOn contact, the bottle will break, releasing a purple gas cloud that \u003cb\u003eintoxicates\u003c/b\u003e Survivors. \u003cb\u003eIntoxicated\u003c/b\u003e Survivors will suffer from impaired vision, involuntary coughing, and \u003cb\u003e14% Hindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e1.6 second\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Afterpiece Antidote\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOn contact, the bottle will break, releasing a gray gas cloud which turns yellow upon activation. The Clown and any Survivors who enter an active \u003cb\u003eAntidote cloud\u003c/b\u003e gain \u003cb\u003e12% Haste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6 seconds\u003c/b\u003e. \u003cb\u003eIntoxicated\u003c/b\u003e Survivors who enter an \u003cb\u003eAntidote cloud\u003c/b\u003e are cured.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/51/IconPowers_gasBomb.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thedarklord","name":"The Dark Lord","bio":"The Dark Lord, Dracula, is the embodiment of darkness and tragedy.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHex: Wretched Fate\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHuman Greed\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eDominance\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to slow the Obsession\u0027s repair speed, see the auras of unopened chests, and block chests and totems.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/62/K37_TheDarkLord_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dominance","description":"The first time each Chest is being unlocked and each Totem is being blessed or cleansed by a Survivor, it is blocked for \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8d/IconPerks_Dominance.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Wretched Fate","description":"The first time a Generator is completed, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Obsession:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eRepairs \u003cb\u003e27/30/33\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSees the Hex Totem\u0027s Aura within \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003em.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/81/IconPerks_HexWretchedFate.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Human Greed","description":"Whenever a Survivor gets within \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003em of a locked Chest, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou can lock unlocked Chests. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see the Auras of locked Chests.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/06/IconPerks_HumanGreed.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/06/PerkAnimation_HumanGreed.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Vampiric Shift","description":"His dark power allows him to exact revenge on humans, taking many forms to terrorize and slaughter them.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: SHAPESHIFT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Dark Lord has access to three Forms and can freely change between them. Each Form has unique abilities and strengths.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eVampire Form:\u003c/b\u003e In his default state, The Dark Lord can use the powerful Hellfire spell, which creates 8 pillars of flame that erupt from the ground in front of him and can be cast across low obstacles.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eWolf Form:\u003c/b\u003e In Wolf Form, The Dark Lord has access to several abilities that allow for more effective tracking. Pools of blood and scratch marks are brighter and running Survivors leave a trail of Scent Orbs behind them. The Dark Lord can collect these Scent Orbs to gain Haste, and charge a powerful Pounce attack to damage Survivors. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eBat Form:\u003c/b\u003e While in Bat Form, The Dark Lord gains the \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e status effect. Additionally, he moves faster, ignores vault points, and can Teleport to any vault points within 32 meters. Survivors become invisible, but scratch marks can be se","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a9/IconPowers_K37_Shapeshift.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thedeathslinger","name":"The Deathslinger","bio":"A vengeful Killer, able to spear Survivors from a distance and Reel them in using his power, \u003cb\u003eThe Redeemer\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eGear Head\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDead Man’s Switch\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHex: Retribution\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to locate and impede Survivor objectives, and punish Survivors for destroying Totems.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ac/K19_TheDeathslinger_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dead Man’s Switch","description":"When you hook a Survivor, the first time a Survivor stops repairing a Generator, it is blocked for \u003cb\u003e25/30/35\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e25/30/35\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c3/IconPerks_deadMansSwitch.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Gearhead","description":"Whenever a Survivor takes damage, for the next \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es, whenever a Survivor repairing a Generator hits a good basic Skill Check, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fd/IconPerks_gearhead.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Retribution","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor starts blessing or cleansing a Totem, they gain \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Hex Totem is blessed or cleansed, you see the Auras of all Survivors for \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ab/IconPerks_hexRetribution.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"The Redeemer","description":"The Deathslinger’s ingenuity affords him the ability to Reel in bounties with a unique invention—a heavily modified, hybrid rifle that replaces conventional ammunition with a razor-sharp spear affixed to a chain.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eTHE REDEEMER\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to aim down sights. Press the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to shoot a spear that can lodge itself in a Survivor, allowing them to be Reeled in towards \u003cb\u003eThe Deathslinger\u003c/b\u003e against their will.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eReel:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile a Survivor is speared by \u003cb\u003eThe Redeemer\u003c/b\u003e, press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to Reel them in towards you. Survivors may struggle against the chain or use the environment to pressure the chain to break. Doing so will result in briefly stunning \u003cb\u003eThe Deathslinger\u003c/b\u003e as well as putting The Survivor in the injured state and applying the \u003cb\u003eDeep Wound\u003c/b\u003e status effect. Using a \u003ci\u003ebasic attack\u003c/i\u003e while a Survivor is speared will break the chain without applying a penalty to either \u003cb\u003eThe Deathslinger\u003c/b\u003e or The Survivor. Successfully hitting a Survivor with a \u003ci\u003ebasic attack\u003c/i\u003e while they are speared and healthy will also apply the \u003cb\u003eDeep Wound\u003c/b\u003e status effect.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eReload:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe Redeemer\u003c/b\u003e must be Reloaded after every shot, before it may be fired again. Press the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to Reload \u003cb\u003eThe Redeemer\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6e/IconPowers_theRedeemer.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thedemogorgon","name":"The Demogorgon","bio":"An unidentified Killer, able to open multiple Portals and traverse between them to cover large distances. Using its power, \u003cb\u003eOf the Abyss\u003c/b\u003e, it can detect any Survivors within a close proximity to the Portals then unleash a leaping attack to inflict damage from a distance.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIts perks, \u003cb\u003eSurge\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCruel Limits\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eMindbreaker\u003c/b\u003e, impact the environment close to generators and affect nearby Survivors in unexpected ways.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/75/K17_TheDemogorgon_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Cruel Limits","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of all Windows for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAll Windows are blocked for Survivors for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c6/IconPerks_cruelLimits.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Mindbreaker","description":"While Survivors are repairing a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eBlindness\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen they stop repairing a Generator, this ends after \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0f/IconPerks_mindbreaker.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Surge","description":"Whenever you down a Survivor with a basic-attack, Generators within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eExplode, lose \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003e% progress and start regressing.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivor repairing them scream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/IconPerks_surge.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Of the Abyss","description":"An unknown and otherworldly power surged through its body. Suddenly the ground ripped open, swallowing The Demogorgon whole.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eOF THE ABYSS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to fully charge and activate \u003cb\u003eOf the Abyss\u003c/b\u003e. All Survivors within a close proximity to an activated Portal will be indicated by Killer Instinct.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: SHRED\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e while charging or holding \u003cb\u003eOf the Abyss\u003c/b\u003e to dive forward and unleash a vicious slash. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: PORTALS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to open a Portal on the ground in front of you.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eTraverse Upside Down:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile standing on a placed Portal with a different Portal highlighted, press the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e again to travel through the Upside Down to arrive at the targeted Portal. Emerging from a Portal grants Undetectable.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eActivated Portals:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePortals become \u0027activated\u0027 when they are first traversed to or from. Only activated Portals may be sealed by Survivors. Activated Portal auras are highlighted in yellow.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a9/IconPowers_ofTheAbyss.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thedoctor","name":"The Doctor","bio":"A madness-inducing Killer who is able to use his power, \u003cb\u003eCarter\u0027s Spark\u003c/b\u003e, to trigger electrical charges, incapacitating Survivors and eventually causing them to hallucinate and scream in terror, revealing their position.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eOverwhelming Presence\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eMonitor \u0026 Abuse\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eOvercharge\u003c/b\u003e, encourage chases, impact Survivors\u0027 ability to repair effectively, and make him harder to detect when not in a chase.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/58/K07_TheDoctor_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Monitor \u0026 Abuse","description":"While chasing a Survivor, your Terror Radius is \u003cb\u003e5/10/15\u003c/b\u003e% bigger.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile not chasing a Survivor, your Terror Radius is \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003e% smaller.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/60/IconPerks_monitorAndAbuse.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/12/Perk-doctor-1.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Overcharge","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eIts regression speed will go from \u003cb\u003e85\u003c/b\u003e% to \u003cb\u003e130\u003c/b\u003e% over the next \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe next Survivor who starts repairing it gets a special Skill Check. If they miss it, they lose \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c3/IconPerks_overcharge.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/14/Overcharge_Success.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Overwhelming Presence","description":"Whenever a Survivor uses an item within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em of you, they gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em of you gains \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e, you see the closest \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e Survivor\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9a/IconPerks_overwhelmingPresence.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/80/Perk-doctor-2.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Carter\u0027s Spark","description":"\u003cb\u003eCARTER\u0027S SPARK\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSuccessfully striking Survivors with \u003cb\u003eThe Doctor\u0027s\u003c/b\u003e special abilities, \u003cb\u003eShock Therapy\u003c/b\u003e or \u003cb\u003eStatic Blast\u003c/b\u003e, increases the Survivor\u0027s \u003ci\u003eMadness\u003c/i\u003e, eventually afflicting them with the \u003cb\u003eMadness\u003c/b\u003e status effect and triggering increasingly potent effects.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eMadness I:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCauses Survivors to scream once, revealing their position to \u003cb\u003eThe Doctor\u003c/b\u003e. \u003cb\u003eSlightly\u003c/b\u003e affects Skill Check placement and direction.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eMadness II:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCauses Survivors to scream once and experience hallucinations in the form of an \u003ci\u003eillusionary Doctor\u003c/i\u003e. \u003cb\u003eModerately\u003c/b\u003e affects Skill Check placement and direction.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eMadness III:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCauses Survivors to scream intermittently and experience hallucinations in the form of an \u003ci\u003eillusionary Doctor\u003c/i\u003e. \u003cb\u003eTremendously\u003c/b\u003e affects Skill Check placement and direction. The Survivor cannot heal, repair, sabotage, unlock, cleanse, or use items until they successfully \u003ci\u003eSnap Out Of It\u003c/i\u003e. When a Survivor completes the \u003ci\u003eSnap Out Of It\u003c/i\u003e action, they return to \u003cb\u003eMadness I\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Shock Therapy\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to perform \u003cb\u003eShock Therapy\u003c/b\u003e, unleashing a ranged shock attack on the ground in front of you. Survivors struck by \u003cb\u003eShock Therapy\u003c/b\u003e gain increased \u003ci\u003eMadness\u003c/i\u003e and any interactions they are performing are immediately interrupted. \u003cb\u003eShock Therapy\u003c/b\u003e immediately negates the \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e status effect.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Static Blast\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to perform a \u003cb\u003eStatic Blast\u003c/b\u003e, causing all Survivors within The Doctor\u0027s Terror Radius to scream and gain increased \u003ci\u003eMadness\u003c/i\u003e. \u003cb\u003eStatic Blast\u003c/b\u003e can only be activated when not on cooldown. \u003cb\u003eStatic Blast\u003c/b\u003e immediately negates the \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e status effect.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/50/IconPowers_cartersSpark.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thedredge","name":"The Dredge","bio":"A manifestation of the dark thoughts of a once-vibrant community, the Dredge is able to teleport between lockers and summon an overwhelming darkness.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIts personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDissolution\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDarkness Revealed\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eSeptic Touch\u003c/b\u003e allow it to destroy pallets, spot Survivors near lockers, and afflict healing Survivors with Blindness and Exhausted.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7e/K28_TheDredge_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Darkness Revealed","description":"Whenever you search a Locker, you see the Auras of Survivors within \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003em of Lockers for \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ed/IconPerks_darknessRevealed.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Dissolution","description":"\u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es after a Survivor takes damage, for \u003cb\u003e12/16/20\u003c/b\u003es, the next time a Survivor fast-vaults a Pallet while within your Terror Radius, it is destroyed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1d/IconPerks_dissolution.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Septic Touch","description":"While a Survivor within your Terror Radius is healing:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eBlindness\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen they stop healing, this ends after \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d8/IconPerks_septicTouch.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Reign of Darkness","description":"Like a dark thought, The Dredge is difficult to shake. And when night falls, it is nearly impossible.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: THE GLOAMING\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to activate. Once activated, The Dredge leaves a Remnant behind. Aim at a locker and press the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e to Teleport into it or press the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to return to the Remnant. The Remnant is disabled when teleporting to a locker, or when a Survivor touches it. While in a locker, aim at any other locker and press the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e to Teleport again. Each Teleport consumes a Power Token. Exiting the locker or returning to your Remnant will activate The Gloaming\u0027s cooldown, after which all Power Tokens are recharged.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors can place locks on lockers to slow The Dredge exiting them. The Dredge can break locks by exiting the locked locker or performing a base attack on the lock. Each locker can only be locked once.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: NIGHTFALL\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe \u003cb\u003eNightfall Meter\u003c/b\u003e builds when a healthy Survivor is injured, a Survivor is hooked, or the Teleport power is used. The \u003cb\u003eNightfall Meter\u003c/b\u003e also fills faster for each Survivor in the injured state. Once the \u003cb\u003eNightfall Meter\u003c/b\u003e is full, \u003cb\u003eNightfall\u003c/b\u003e begins.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDuring \u003cb\u003eNightfall\u003c/b\u003e, Survivors must navigate in total darkness, The Dredge’s Teleport is faster with a shorter cooldown, and gains Undetectable. \u003cb\u003eNightfall\u003c/b\u003e ends after 60 seconds.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/49/IconPowers_reignOfDarkness.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theexecutioner","name":"The Executioner","bio":"A map-manipulation Killer, able to torment Survivors with the hazards he creates. Affected Survivors will be vulnerable to his special hook, the \u003cb\u003eCage of Atonement\u003c/b\u003e, and his unique mori, \u003cb\u003eFinal Judgment\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eForced Penance\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eTrail of Torment\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eDeathbound\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to aggressively pursue his prey while deceiving and tracking Survivors.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c9/K20_TheExecutioner_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Deathbound","description":"Whenever a Survivor finishes healing another, the healer screams. Then, until the healer takes damage, while they are at least \u003cb\u003e12/8/4\u003c/b\u003em away from the healed Survivor:\u003cli\u003eThe healer gains \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe healer sees the healed Survivor\u0027s Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis can only apply to one Survivor at a time.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e7/IconPerks_deathbound.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Forced Penance","description":"Whenever a Survivor takes a protection hit, they gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/70/80\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1d/IconPerks_forcedPenance.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Trail of Torment","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, until it stops regressing:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eundetectable\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors see that Generator\u0027s Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/45/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/94/IconPerks_trailOfTorment.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Rites of Judgment","description":"Open the gates of suffering and be judged! The Great Knife splits the ground, giving rise to an infernal construct and spreading agony to all who approach.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eRITES OF JUDGMENT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to activate, then move in any direction to carve a trail into the ground.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors who walk or run on the trail will trigger \u003ci\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/i\u003e and be afflicted with \u003ci\u003eTorment\u003c/i\u003e. Survivors affected by \u003ci\u003eTorment\u003c/i\u003e may be sent to a \u003cb\u003eCage of Atonement\u003c/b\u003e while they are in the dying state.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: Punishment of the Damned\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e while \u003cb\u003eRites of Judgment\u003c/b\u003e is active to perform \u003cb\u003ePunishment of the Damned\u003c/b\u003e. This unleashes a wave of force, damaging any Survivors in its path.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Cage of Atonement\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e while standing over a dying Survivor suffering from \u003ci\u003eTorment\u003c/i\u003e to send them to a \u003cb\u003eCage of Atonement\u003c/b\u003e. Survivors in a \u003cb\u003eCage of Atonement\u003c/b\u003e can be sacrificed as if they were on a hook. During the second phase of the summoning ritual they will be forced to complete Skill Checks to hold off The Entity.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBeing rescued or rescuing another Survivor from a \u003cb\u003eCage of Atonement\u003c/b\u003e will remove \u003ci\u003eTorment\u003c/i\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Final Judgment\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e when standing over a dying Survivor suffering from \u003ci\u003eTorment\u003c/i\u003e who has already reached struggle phase on a hook or in a cage to execute them.","icon":null}},{"id":"thefirst","name":"The First","bio":"The First is a cunning and cruel former test subject, whose powers were sharpened in an alternate dimension.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eTurn Back The Clock\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSecret Project\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHex: Hive Mind\u003c/b\u003e allow him to damage distant generators, block them from repair, and set them back when another is completed.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"Hex: Hive Mind","description":"The first time you hook a Survivor, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Auras of Generators show their progress.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Generator remains:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAll Generators explode, lose \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003e% progress and start regressing.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Hex Totem is extinguished.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Secret Project","description":"Whenever a Totem is blessed or cleansed, a random unblocked Generator is blocked for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever 1 or more Generators are blocked, you gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Turn Back The Clock","description":"After hooking a Survivor, for the next \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to make target Generator you can see within \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003em explode, lose \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e% progress and start regressing.\u003cbr\u003e","icon":null,"video":null}],"power":{"name":"Test Subject #001","description":"\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: VINE ATTACK\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the Power button to charge a Vine Attack. When charged, press the Attack button to activate it, creating a small area of effect on the ground.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAny Survivors caught within the area of the Vine Attack earn a Worldbreaker token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: THE UPSIDE DOWN \u0026 UNDERGATE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Killer can enter The Upside Down to navigate the map quickly by tapping the Ability button. While in The Upside Down, the Killer can activate an Undergate attack to return to the map, creating a large area of effect on the ground. Survivors caught within its radius gain 2 Worldbreaker tokens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL CONDITION/ITEM: WORLDBREAKER \u0026 GRANDFATHER CLOCKS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOnce a Survivor has gained enough tokens, Worldbreaker activates, and the Worldbreaker Timer begins. While Worldbreaker is active, both the Vine Attack and Undergate attacks do damage to Survivors instead of adding Worldbreaker tokens, and 4 Grandfather Clocks activate.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWorldbreaker lasts for a predetermined amount of time, based on the number of Survivors alive. Survivors can interact with the Grandfather Clocks spread around the map to speed up the Worldbreaker Timer.","icon":null}},{"id":"theghostface","name":"The Ghost Face","bio":"A creepy Killer, able to Stalk his victims and sneak up silently using his power, \u003cb\u003eNight Shroud\u003c/b\u003e. Affected Survivors will find themselves vulnerable and oblivious to his presence and must use all of their perception and awareness to protect themselves from his approach.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eI\u0027m All Ears\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eThrilling Tremors\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eFurtive Chase\u003c/b\u003e, give him the ability to locate Survivors, defend generators, and make his chases unpredictable.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d1/K16_TheGhostFace_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Furtive Chase","description":"Whenever you hook the Obsession:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e14/16/18\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e14/16/18\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever the Obsession is unhooked, the Survivor who unhooked them becomes the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/94/IconPerks_furtiveChase.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"I\u0027m All Ears","description":"Whenever a Survivor fast-enters or fast-exits a Locker, or medium or fast-vaults within \u003cb\u003e48\u003c/b\u003em of you, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/45/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e3/IconPerks_imAllEars.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/74/IAE-Q%26Q.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Thrilling Tremors","description":"Whenever you pick-up a Survivor, all Generators not being repaired are blocked for \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b8/IconPerks_thrillingTremors.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Night Shroud","description":"\u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u003c/b\u003e used to study his victims for weeks, meticulously registering their habits. When the urge to kill swelled, he’d know exactly how and where to strike.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eNIGHT SHROUD\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to activate \u003cb\u003eNight Shroud\u003c/b\u003e when the power gauge is full. \u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u003c/b\u003e is granted the \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e status effect while \u003cb\u003eNight Shroud\u003c/b\u003e is active. Performing a \u003ci\u003ebasic attack\u003c/i\u003e fully depletes the power gauge and deactivates \u003cb\u003eNight Shroud\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eReveal:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors within proximity to \u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u003c/b\u003e may attempt to \u003ci\u003ereveal\u003c/i\u003e him by looking in his direction for a short duration. A successful \u003ci\u003ereveal\u003c/i\u003e fully depletes \u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u0027s\u003c/b\u003e power gauge and automatically deactivates \u003cb\u003eNight Shroud\u003c/b\u003e. Survivors who \u003ci\u003ereveal\u003c/i\u003e \u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u003c/b\u003e have their current location indicated by \u003ci\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/i\u003e for a very short duration.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: STALK\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHold down the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to Stalk Survivors while \u003cb\u003eNight Shroud\u003c/b\u003e is active. Hold down the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e while behind cover to lean out and Stalk at a faster rate. Completing Stalk progress on a Survivor \u003ci\u003eMarks\u003c/i\u003e your target and applies the \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e status effect to your \u003ci\u003eMark\u003c/i\u003e for a limited amount of time. \u003ci\u003eMarked\u003c/i\u003e Survivors cannot \u003ci\u003ereveal\u003c/i\u003e \u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: CROUCH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the Active Ability button to Crouch. Press the Active Ability button again while Crouched to stand. \u003cb\u003eThe Ghost Face\u003c/b\u003e moves at a slower speed while Crouched.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/27/IconPowers_nightShroud.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theghoul","name":"The Ghoul","bio":"The Ghoul has been pushed to his limits and he’s hungry for more.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHex: Nothing But Misery\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eForever Entwined\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eNone Are Free\u003c/b\u003e, help him Hinder Survivors, hook Survivors more quickly, and block pallets when all generators are completed.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c9/K39_TheGhoul_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Forever Entwined","description":"Whenever a Survivor takes damage, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou hook Survivors \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou pick-up and drop Survivors \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6d/IconPerks_foreverEntwined.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Nothing But Misery","description":"After you damage Survivors with a basic-attack \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003e times, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you damage a Survivor with a basic-attack, they gain \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e10/12.5/15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6f/IconPerks_hexNothingButMisery.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"None Are Free","description":"The first time you hook each Survivor, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all Generators are completed, for each Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eUpright Pallets are blocked for \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWindows are blocked for \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5c/IconPerks_noneAreFree.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"One-Eyed Terror","description":"\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Kagune Leap\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUse the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge and launch the \u003cb\u003eKagune\u003c/b\u003e, tentacles that attach to any vertical surface within range and quickly pull The Ghoul forward.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter completing a \u003cb\u003eleap\u003c/b\u003e, The Ghoul has a window to perform a second consecutive \u003cb\u003eKagune Leap\u003c/b\u003e or put \u003cb\u003eKagune Leap\u003c/b\u003e into cooldown by using the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eKagune Leap\u003c/b\u003e enters cooldown once The Ghoul has consumed their \u003cb\u003eleaps\u003c/b\u003e, if they \u003cb\u003eleap\u003c/b\u003e and special-vault a window or dropped pallet, or if the \u003cb\u003eKagune\u003c/b\u003e grabs and \u003cb\u003eleaps\u003c/b\u003e at a Survivor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf The Ghoul\u0027s second consecutive \u003cb\u003eleap\u003c/b\u003e targets a Survivor, they will perform a grab-attack. Grab-attacks damage Survivors if they are healthy; inflict \u003cb\u003eDeep Wounds\u003c/b\u003e; and leave a \u003cb\u003eKagune Mark\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePerforming a grab-attack also triggers \u003cb\u003eEnraged Mode\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Enraged Mode\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile \u003cb\u003eEnraged\u003c/b\u003e, The Ghoul can perform up to three consecutive \u003cb\u003eKagune Leaps\u003c/b\u003e and can special-vault faster if they launch their \u003cb\u003eKagune\u003c/b\u003e at a Survivor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eEnraged Mode\u003c/b\u003e remains active while there are Survivors afflicted with \u003cb\u003eKagune Mark\u003c/b\u003e. Marked Survivors will lose their mark if they are fully \u003cb\u003emended\u003c/b\u003e, or if they are downed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Ghoul cannot grab-attack marked Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOnce no marked Survivors remain, a \u003cb\u003eCountdown\u003c/b\u003e begins. When the \u003cb\u003eCountdown\u003c/b\u003e depletes, \u003cb\u003eEnraged Mode\u003c/b\u003e ends. A perfectly timed grab-attack - tapping the \u003ci\u003eattack button\u003c/i\u003e when the attack icon is displayed - will add extra time to the \u003cb\u003eCountdown\u003c/b\u003e. The \u003cb\u003eCountdown\u003c/b\u003e is paused while carrying Survivors.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/77/IconPowers_oneEyedTerror.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thegoodguy","name":"The Good Guy","bio":"The Good Guy is an elusive Killer, capable of deceiving Survivors with his illusory Footfalls and deadly \u003cb\u003eSlice \u0026 Dice\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHex: Two Can Play\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eFriends \u0027til the End\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBatteries Included\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to blind those who blind him, relentlessly hunt his Obsession, and get faster around completed generators.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/81/K34_TheGoodGuy_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Batteries Included","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em of a completed Generator, you gain \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e. When you leave the range, this ends after \u003cb\u003e1/3/5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1c/IconPerks_batteriesIncluded.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Friends ‘Til the End","description":"Whenever you Hook a Survivor that is not the Obsession:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Obsession gains \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Obsession\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you Hook the Obsession, another Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eScreams, then you are alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBecomes the Obsession.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b3/IconPerks_friendsTilTheEnd.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Two Can Play","description":"While this Hex is dull, each time you are blinded or stunned by a Survivor \u003cb\u003e4/3/2\u003c/b\u003e times, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you are blinded or stunned by a Survivor you are not carrying, they are blinded for \u003cb\u003e1.5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/64/IconPerks_hexTwoCanPlay.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Playtime\u0027s Over","description":"After the rage of being trapped in the body of a doll subsided, the Lakeshore Strangler realized this new body was the perfect host to disorient and surprise his kills.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: HIDEY-HO MODE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eChucky can enter \u003cb\u003eHidey-Ho Mode\u003c/b\u003e at any time, provided the cooldown is over. When in \u003cb\u003eHidey-Ho Mode\u003c/b\u003e, Chucky becomes \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e and generates map-wide Footfalls, disorienting Survivors with sounds and footprints coming from many directions.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: SLICE \u0026 DICE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile in \u003cb\u003eHidey-Ho Mode\u003c/b\u003e, Chucky gets access to the charged \u003cb\u003eSlice \u0026 Dice\u003c/b\u003e ability, allowing him to rush unsuspecting Survivors before leaping forward and performing a \u003cb\u003eSlice \u0026 Dice attack\u003c/b\u003e. Additionally, Chucky can quickly chain a \u003cb\u003eScamper\u003c/b\u003e while using a \u003cb\u003eSlice \u0026 Dice\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: SCAMPER\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile performing a \u003cb\u003eSlice \u0026 Dice\u003c/b\u003e in \u003cb\u003eHidey-Ho Mode\u003c/b\u003e, Chucky can perform a \u003cb\u003eScamper\u003c/b\u003e and special-vault over a window or under a downed pallet, allowing him to close on his unsuspecting prey.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e“I\u0027m one of the most notorious slashers in history. And I don\u0027t want to give that up. I am Chucky, the killer doll! And I dig it!” – Chucky","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bd/IconPowers_playtimesOver.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thehag","name":"The Hag","bio":"A cursed Killer, able to place traps and then Teleport to them when activated, using her \u003cb\u003eBlackened Catalyst\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHex: The Third Seal\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Ruin\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eHex: Devour Hope\u003c/b\u003e, apply crippling penalties to Survivors as long as the Totem they are attached to remains uncleansed.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c7/K06_TheHag_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Hex: Devour Hope","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor is unhooked while you are at least \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em away, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e2 Tokens | \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es after hooking a Survivor, gain \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e3 Tokens | Survivors gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e5 Tokens | You can Kill downed Survivors.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c9/IconPerks_hexDevourHope.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Ruin","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile a Generator is not being repaired, it regresses at \u003cb\u003e100/125/150\u003c/b\u003e% speed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a2/IconPerks_hexRuin.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/66/Ruin_Failure.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hex: The Third Seal","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you damage a Survivor with a basic or special-attack, they gain \u003cb\u003eBlindness\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis applies for up to \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e Survivors.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/36/IconPerks_hexTheThirdSeal.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Blackened Catalyst","description":"The source of The Hag\u0027s power, a blackened finger used as a catalyst for her terrible power. The Hag bends and shapes mud to her will. With simple ritualistic drawings, she creates deceitful duplicates of herself made from mud and decay which she can use for various effects.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGrants the ability to create and maintain \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e Phantasm Traps.Grants the ability to instantly travel to triggered Phantasm Traps when within a \u003cb\u003e48 meter\u003c/b\u003e range.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/62/IconPowers_blackenedCatalyst.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thehillbilly","name":"The Hillbilly","bio":"A high-mobility Killer, able to cover large distances in a short amount of time and instantly down Survivors using his \u003cb\u003eChainsaw\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eEnduring\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eLightborn\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eTinkerer\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to enhance his power and make him harder to lose during chases.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/24/K03_TheHillbilly_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Enduring","description":"While not carrying a Survivor, Pallet-stuns are \u003cb\u003e40/45/50\u003c/b\u003e% shorter.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/94/IconPerks_enduring.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ee/Enduring.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Lightborn","description":"Whenever a Survivor attempts to blind you, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou cannot be blinded.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/48/IconPerks_lightborn.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Tinkerer","description":"The first time each Generator has \u003cb\u003e70\u003c/b\u003e% progress:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou are alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d9/IconPerks_tinkerer.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1b/Tinkerer.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Chainsaw","description":"\u003ci\u003eThe machine gave him a new life, one where the power was in his hands.\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to break into a \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sprint\u003c/b\u003e. Survivors hit during a \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sprint\u003c/b\u003e are put into the dying state. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eRevving the chainsaw, and sprinting each cause the \u003cb\u003eOverdrive meter\u003c/b\u003e to increase. The meter decreases when the chainsaw is not in use.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the meter is full, the chainsaw goes into \u003cb\u003eOverdrive\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL STATE: OVERDRIVE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile in \u003cb\u003eOverdrive\u003c/b\u003e, the chainsaw is enhanced. Chainsaw Charge and Sprint speeds are increased, and \u003cb\u003eChainsaw Sprint\u003c/b\u003e cooldowns are reduced.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eOverdrive\u003c/b\u003e lasts for \u003cb\u003e20 seconds\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b1/IconPowers_chainsaw.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thehoundmaster","name":"The Houndmaster","bio":"The Houndmaster is a force to be feared, with an equally fearsome dog at her side.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eAll-Shaking Thunder\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eScourge Hook: Jagged Compass\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eNo Quarter\u003c/b\u003e, help her increase her lunge attack distance, create scourge hooks, and overwhelm Survivors with healing Skill Checks.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/96/K38_TheHoundmaster_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"All-Shaking Thunder","description":"Whenever you fall from at least \u003cb\u003e1.25\u003c/b\u003em, your lunge-attacks are \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% longer for \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6a/IconPerks_allShakingThunder.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"No Quarter","description":"While self-healing, whenever a Survivor has \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% progress, they get special Skill Checks. If they miss one of these or stop healing, they gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c3/IconPerks_noQuarter.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Scourge Hook: Jagged Compass","description":"When the trial starts, 4 random Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor is unhooked, the Hook becomes a Scourge Hook.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you hook a Survivor on a Scourge Hook, for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es, you see the Aura of the Generator with the most progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/53/IconPerks_scourgeHookJaggedCompass.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Scent of Blood","description":"The Houndmaster and her dog operate as one. Her commands are followed without question or delay.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: CHASE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Chase Command sends the dog out at high speed. Pressing the Power button again redirects the Chase, pivoting the dog\u0027s path. When the dog catches a Survivor, the dog starts a Grab. The Survivor becomes \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e and is pulled toward The Houndmaster. The Survivor can get free by stunning the dog or can be rescued by another Survivor. Grabs that end without injury leave the Survivor \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e. Grab duration is shorter for Survivors with the \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e status effect.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: SEARCH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Search Command sends the dog to a target location, creating a Search Path. It has its own lullaby and, as it moves, its Houndsense radius rises over distance traveled. Survivors who enter the radius are affected by Houndsense and revealed by Killer Instinct. If The Houndmaster follows the dog’s Search Path, she gains increased movement speed over time. Leaving the Search Path ends the bonus movement speed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL EFFECT: HOUNDSENSE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHealthy Survivors affected by Houndsense receive \u003cb\u003eDeep Wounds\u003c/b\u003e when injured. Injured Survivors affected by Houndsense suffer from louder grunts of pain and longer pools of blood when put into the dying sta","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/df/IconPowers_scentOfBlood.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thehuntress","name":"The Huntress","bio":"A ranged Killer, able to throw \u003cb\u003eHunting Hatchets\u003c/b\u003e at Survivors to injure them from a distance.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBeast of Prey\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eTerritorial Imperative\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eHex: Huntress Lullaby\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to apply pressure through better map awareness and enhanced chasing abilities.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f1/K08_TheHuntress_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Beast of Prey","description":"Whenever you gain Bloodlust, gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30/35/40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/77/IconPerks_beastOfPrey.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6d/Killer-perk2.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hex: Huntress Lullaby","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you hook a Survivor, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token. For each Token, Basic Skill Check warnings appear later and good success zones are smaller.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile you have \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, Basic Skill Check warnings don\u0027t appear.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor misses a basic Skill Check, they lose \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/11/IconPerks_hexHuntressLullaby.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cd/Killer-perk3.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Territorial Imperative","description":"Whenever a Survivor enters the Basement while you are \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em away from it, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e45\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2a/IconPerks_territorialImperative.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b7/Killer-perk1.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Hunting Hatchets","description":"A skill taught by her mother and mastered in the wild. The Huntress can hurl Hatchets with deadly precision.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eStart the trial with \u003cb\u003e7 Hatchets\u003c/b\u003e.Charge throw for maximum throwing speed.Refill Hatchets at \u003cb\u003eLockers\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e5/IconPowers_huntingHatchets.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thejudgment","name":"The Judgment","bio":"The Judgment enforces the will of The Creators with Its Divine Light.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIts personal perks, \u003cb\u003eCelestial Witness\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Under Your Thumb\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eLay Waste\u003c/b\u003e, allow It to track the Obsession, limit and surveil Survivors with Haste, and increase generator regression.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/97/K44_TheJudgment_Portrait.webp/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Celestial Witness","description":"Every \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es, if the Obsession is at least \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003em away from you, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e2/2.5/3\u003c/b\u003es. Otherwise, the farthest Survivor becomes the Obsession.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Hex: Under Your Thumb","description":"The first time a Survivor gains a Hook State, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a running Survivor gains \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em of you, you are alerted.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eRunning Survivors cannot gain more than \u003cb\u003e25/20/15\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e at a time.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Lay Waste","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, for each Charge it has, it regresses \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e% faster. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e55/50/45\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null}],"power":{"name":"Will of the Gods","description":"\u003cb\u003eDIVINE LIGHT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the Power button to Charge Will of The Gods and call upon Divine Light, allowing The Judgment to control its trajectory for a moment.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDivine Light passes through all obstacles, at a slightly lower speed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen The Judgment is ready, they can Cast Divine Light, sending forth, becoming lethal and gaining constant speed, unaffected by obstacles.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe longer Divine Light is controlled, the stronger the Cast action will be, increasing its acceleration, duration, and becoming lethal more quickly.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAnytime a Survivor is caught in a Cast Divine Light’s trajectory, if they are not a Heretic, they gain Heresy and lose a health state.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eHERESY\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen a Survivor is damaged by Divine Light, they gain Heresy, which makes their repairs less efficient, causing loss of progress on Good Repair Skillcheck.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHeresy will decay over time after Repenting at a Shrine of Judgment, when Liberating Heretics from Exile or when saved from the Exile.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eEXILE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen standing over a Survivor affected by Heresy, The Judgment can Exile them or Kill them if they are on their second hook, gaining Zealous.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen Exiled, they gain a Hook State and must dodge Seeds of Punishment, which seek to purify the Exile of their presence. While in Exile, Survivors can use the Searcher’s Pendant to collect Exiled Souls, which grant them bonus protections when saved from the Exile by Survivors who liberate them at a Shrine of Judgment.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eZEALOUS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile Zealous, The Judgment gains the ability to quickly redirect Divine Light after casting it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDivine Light is also larger and faster.","icon":null}},{"id":"theknight","name":"The Knight","bio":"The Knight is a strategic Killer, able to send his faithful Guards to hunt for Survivors and damage objects on the battlefield.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eNowhere to Hide\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Face the Darkness\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHubris\u003c/b\u003e allow him to reveal Survivors near generators, curse Survivors to scream out in fear, and cause a Survivor who stuns you to become Exposed.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/69/K30_TheKnight_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Hex: Face the Darkness","description":"Whenever you damage a Survivor, they are hexed and a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEvery \u003cb\u003e35/30/25\u003c/b\u003es, other Survivors not within your Terror Radius scream, then you see their Auras for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the hexed Survivor is downed or becomes healthy, the Hex Totem is extinguished.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/af/IconPerks_hexFaceTheDarkness.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hubris","description":"Whenever you are stunned by a Survivor, they gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/aa/IconPerks_hubris.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/af/Hubris_Activating.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Nowhere to Hide","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es, you see the Auras of Survivors within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em of it.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/29/IconPerks_nowhereToHide.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Guardia Compagnia","description":"The Knight alone is a terrifying monster on the battlefield, but with his loyal Guards, he is nearly unstoppable. Together, the Guardia Compagnia fights for their own freedom, killing anyone who gets in their way.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: GUARD SUMMON\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTap the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to activate Guard Summon mode. Once activated, move around to create a Patrol Path. While in Guard Summon mode, you can aim at a generator in progress, a dropped pallet or a breakable wall and tap the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e. This will summon a Guard to damage or special-break the selected object.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou can also tap the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e or drain the Power Gauge completely to end the Guard Summon mode. This will summon a Guard who will follow and Patrol the created Path. The longer the Patrol Path, the longer the Guard\u0027s Hunt Timer will be. There are three Guards that can be summoned one at a time: The Carnifex, who can damage or special-break objects faster; The Assassin, who moves faster during the Hunt; and The Jailer, who patrols and hunts longer, and is better at detection.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eGUARD SPECIAL ABILITY: THE HUNT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile a Guard is patrolling, he can spot and detect Survivors. If a Survivor is detected, the Guard will move to their location, leave a Standard on the ground, and start Hunting the Survivor for a set amount of time. The Survivor can escape a Guard by unhooking another Survivor, grabbing the Standard, or surviving until the Hunt timer ends. If the Survivor is successfully attacked by the Guard or The Knight, the Guard will disappear. When a Guard downs a Survivor, The Knight receives a Killer Instinct notification.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d2/IconPowers_guardiaCompagnia.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thekrasue","name":"The Krasue","bio":"A shape-changing Killer, able to inflict Survivors with an effect that weakens them to her Intestinal Whip attack.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eRavenous\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eWandering Eye\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHex: Overture of Doom\u003c/b\u003e help her increase mid-trial pressure, spot injured Survivors, and cause confusion to her whereabouts.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/93/K41_TheKrasue_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Hex: Overture of Doom","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites and hexes the farthest Generator from it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter a Survivor repairs the hexed Generator for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e seconds:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eFor that time, your Terror Radius is set to that Generator.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the hexed Generator is repaired, the next farthest Generator is hexed.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Ravenous","description":"The first time you hook each Survivor, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you have \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, all Survivors:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eScream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Wandering Eye","description":"Whenever you start chasing a Survivor, for the next \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es, you see the Auras of all other injured Survivors within \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003em. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null}],"power":{"name":"Unbodied Flesh","description":"\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: CORPOREAL WEAVE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Krasue can shift between Body and Head Forms at will.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBody Form has a \u003cb\u003e32-meter\u003c/b\u003e Terror Radius. Head Form has a \u003cb\u003e40-meter\u003c/b\u003e Terror Radius. It is slightly faster, can special-vault, but cannot break dropped pallets or gain Bloodlust in chase.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL EFFECT: LEECHED\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHitting a Survivor with \u003cb\u003eIntestinal Whip\u003c/b\u003e or a \u003cb\u003eLeeching Gland\u003c/b\u003e adds to their \u003cb\u003eLeech Meter\u003c/b\u003e. When the meter is filled, the Survivor is afflicted with \u003cb\u003eLeeched I\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cb\u003eLeeched I\u003c/b\u003e: The \u003cb\u003eLeech Meter\u003c/b\u003e fills automatically.\u003cb\u003eLeeched II\u003c/b\u003e: The Survivor is afflicted with \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e. If healthy, they become injured.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: INTESTINAL WHIP\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn Head Form, press the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to lash out with your internal organs.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors afflicted with \u003cb\u003eLeeched\u003c/b\u003e can be damaged by \u003cb\u003eIntestinal Whip\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cb\u003eIntestinal Whip\u003c/b\u003e partially fills a Survivor’s \u003cb\u003eLeech Meter\u003c/b\u003e, up to \u003cb\u003eLeech I\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: REGURGITATE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn Body Form, press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge \u003cb\u003eRegurgitate\u003c/b\u003e. When charged, tap the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to spew a \u003cb\u003eLeeching Gland\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cb\u003eLeeching Gland\u003c/b\u003e completely fills a Survivor’s \u003cb\u003eLeech Meter\u003c/b\u003e, up to \u003cb\u003eLeech I\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ITEM: GLOWING FUNGUS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors can eat \u003cb\u003eGlowing Fungus\u003c/b\u003e to decrease the \u003cb\u003eLeech Meter\u003c/b\u003e over time. Being hit ends the effect.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: HEADLONG FLIGHT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn Head Form, press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to speed through the air.","icon":null}},{"id":"thelegion","name":"The Legion","bio":"A band of merciless Killers, able to rushdown helpless Survivors with their power, \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e. Attacks made during their frenzy inflict lingering internal damage, downing any Survivors that are not quick enough to react.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTheir personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDiscordance\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eMad Grit\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eIron Maiden\u003c/b\u003e, give them the ability to locate their prey and attack savagely while transporting Survivors to the hook.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/53/K14_TheLegion_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Discordance","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e64/96/128\u003c/b\u003em of you, whenever a Generator is being repaired by at least 2 Survivors, you are alerted.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile that Generator is being repaired by at least 2 Survivors, you see its Aura. When it is no longer being repaired by at least 2 Survivors, this ends after \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/82/IconPerks_discordance.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Iron Maiden","description":"Whenever a Survivor exits a Locker:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey scream, then you are alerted to their location for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou open Lockers \u003cb\u003e30/40/50\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b0/IconPerks_ironMaiden.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Mad Grit","description":"While carrying a Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you miss a basic-attack, your cooldown is \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% shorter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you damage a Survivor with a basic attack, the carried Survivor gains no wiggle progress for \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/da/IconPerks_madGrit.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Feral Frenzy","description":"They were a plain group of friends until Frank formed them into a Legion. Now they draw power from the thrilling freedom of not abiding by any rule but their own.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eFERAL FRENZY\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTrigger \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e to run at a high speed and chain attacks between multiple Survivors. When your power gauge is full, press the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to initiate \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e. While \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e is active, \u003cb\u003eThe Legion\u003c/b\u003e moves faster and gains access to additional abilities: \u003cb\u003ePallet Vault\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: PALLET VAULT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eInteraction button\u003c/i\u003e while \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e is active, to \u003cb\u003especial-vault\u003c/b\u003e a dropped pallet.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: FERAL SLASH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e while \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e is active to perform a \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e. Hitting a Survivor with \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e puts the Survivor into the injured state, inflicts the \u003cb\u003eDeep Wound\u003c/b\u003e status effect, and refills \u003cb\u003eThe Legion’s\u003c/b\u003e power gauge. Additionally, any Survivors within the Terror Radius not afflicted by the \u003cb\u003eDeep Wound\u003c/b\u003e status effect are indicated by Killer Instinct. If a Survivor hit by \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e is already afflicted by the \u003cb\u003eDeep Wound\u003c/b\u003e status effect, \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e ends immediately. Each successful \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e that does not end \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e increases \u003cb\u003eThe Legion’s\u003c/b\u003e movement speed by \u003cb\u003e0.24m/s\u003c/b\u003e for the remainder of \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e. The fifth consecutive \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e will put any Survivor into the dying state. The fifth successful \u003cb\u003eFeral Slash\u003c/b\u003e always ends \u003cb\u003eFeral Frenzy\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e8/IconPowers_feralFrenzy.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thelich","name":"The Lich","bio":"Few dare speak The Lich\u0027s true name, for fear that he may hear... or worse.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eWeave Attunement\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eLanguid Touch\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eDark Arrogance\u003c/b\u003e allow him to exploit used items, exhaust those who disturb the crows, and increase vault speed.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f0/K36_TheLich_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dark Arrogance","description":"You basic-vault Windows \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you are blinded or Pallet-stunned, the duration is \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003e% longer.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b1/IconPerks_darkArrogance.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Languid Touch","description":"Whenever a Survivor within \u003cb\u003e36\u003c/b\u003em of you scares a Crow, they gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a3/IconPerks_languidTouch.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Weave Attunement","description":"The first time each item is depleted, it is dropped.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile a Survivor is within \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003em of a dropped item:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see their Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey see the item\u0027s Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor picks-up an item, they gain \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/de/IconPerks_weaveAttunement.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"VILE DARKNESS","description":"Bound with the skin and flesh of men, the Book is packed with spells both forbidden and wicked.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTo select a Spell, hold Ability button 1 to open the Spell selection. The Lich has 4 different Spells:\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eMage Hand: Creates a magical hand that lifts downed pallets or blocks upright pallets for 4 seconds.Flight of the Damned: Conjures 5 flying entities that pass through obstacles and injure Survivors.Dispelling Sphere: Casts a moving invisible sphere that reveals Survivors \u0026 temporarily disables Magic Items.Fly: Briefly move faster, ignoring vaults and pallets.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ITEM: MAGIC ITEMS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTreasure Chests found around the map can contain Magic Items for Survivors to equip. These include Boots/Gauntlets of:\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Interloper: When Mage Hand is used, reveals aura of affected pallets and applies Haste for 4 seconds.The Nightwatch: Reveals auras of Flight of the Damned.The Archivist: Makes Dispelling Sphere visible.The Skyguard: Reveals The Lich\u0027s aura during Fly and for a few seconds after.Additionally, upon procurement, all Magic Items briefly reveal Vecna\u0027s aura.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ITEMS: HAND \u0026 EYE OF VECNA\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eRarely, Treasure Chests contain the Hand or Eye of Vecna. When picked up and used by a Survivor at full health, they cost them a health state, reveal their location with Killer Instinct for 4 seconds, and grant them a special ability.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHand of Vecna: A Fast Locker Entry teleports the Survivor to a further locker.Eye of Vecna: A Fast Locker Exit hides the Survivor\u0027s aura and grants Haste for 12 seconds.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/23/IconPowers_VileDarkness.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"themastermind","name":"The Mastermind","bio":"Albert Wesker is a brilliant and ruthless mastermind infused with the power of Uroboros.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eSuperior Anatomy\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eAwakened Awareness\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTerminus\u003c/b\u003e allow you to vault faster, see other Survivor\u0027s auras while carrying one, and cause Survivors to be permanently Broken when the exit gates are powered.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ec/K29_TheMastermind_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Awakened Awareness","description":"While carrying a Survivor, within \u003cb\u003e16/18/20\u003c/b\u003em of you, you see the Auras of other Survivors.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/97/IconPerks_awakenedAwareness.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Superior Anatomy","description":"Whenever a Survivor fast-vaults within \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003em of you, the next time you basic-vault a window, it is \u003cb\u003e30/35/40\u003c/b\u003e% faster. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4a/IconPerks_superiorAnatomy.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Terminus","description":"When all Generators are completed: all injured, downed, and hooked Survivors gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen an Exit Gate is opened, this ends after \u003cb\u003e35/40/45\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4c/IconPerks_terminus.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Virulent Bound","description":"The Mastermind can barrel forward, Infecting Survivors with the Uroboros virus or leaping over obstacles.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge a \u003cb\u003eBound\u003c/b\u003e attack. While charging, The Mastermind moves slightly slower as he prepares his strike. When charged, press the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to \u003cb\u003eBound\u003c/b\u003e. If The Mastermind hits a Survivor, that Survivor becomes Infected (or furthers their Infection). Should The Mastermind crash into something during this \u003cb\u003eBound\u003c/b\u003e, he will slam the Survivor, causing damage; if not, the Survivor is thrown, losing a health state if they are thrown into any solid object.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf \u003cb\u003eVirulent Bound\u003c/b\u003e hits a window or dropped pallet, The Mastermind will special-vault the obstacle.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL EFFECT: UROBOROS INFECTION\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUpon being hit by \u003cb\u003eVirulent Bound\u003c/b\u003e, Survivors become Infected. Infected builds over time, and when fully Infected, the Survivor suffers from a \u003cb\u003e4% Hindered\u003c/b\u003e status effect. If a \u003cb\u003eVirulent Bound\u003c/b\u003e grabs and slams a Survivor while they are fully Infected, The Mastermind will automatically carry them.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL INTERACTION: FIRST AID SPRAY\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAt the beginning of each trial, several Supply Crates spawn. Each contains a First Aid Spray. When Infected, a Survivor can use the First Aid Spray on themselves or another, removing the Infection. Each First Aid Spray has a set number of charges. After using a First Aid Spray, the Survivor\u0027s location is briefly revealed by Killer Instinct.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1d/IconPowers_virulentBound.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thenemesis","name":"The Nemesis","bio":"An unrelenting Killer, capable of attacking at mid-range with his tentacle, while receiving support from Zombies roaming the area.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eLethal Pursuer\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHysteria\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eEruption\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to quickly ambush Survivors, while sowing confusion and fear when injuring and hooking them.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/67/K24_TheNemesis_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Eruption","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, when you down a Survivor, all Generators damaged this way:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eExplode, lose \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e% progress and start regressing.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors repairing them scream, then you see their Auras for \u003cb\u003e8/10/12\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/dd/IconPerks_eruption.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/59/PerkAnimation_Eruption.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hysteria","description":"Whenever a healthy Survivor becomes injured, all injured Survivors gain \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30/35/40\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3a/IconPerks_hysteria.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Lethal Pursuer","description":"When the trial starts, you see the Auras of all Survivors for \u003cb\u003e7/8/9\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you see a Survivor\u0027s Aura for a duration, it is \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es longer.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/61/IconPerks_lethalPursuer.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"T-VIRUS","description":"A virus that causes extreme mutations and can be transferred to others. Heightens aggression and strength within The Nemesis.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: Tentacle Strike\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge an attack. Once charged, tap the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e. Hitting a Survivor with \u003cb\u003eTentacle Strike\u003c/b\u003e afflicts them with the \u003cb\u003eContaminated\u003c/b\u003e status effect and increases your \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate\u003c/b\u003e. If a Survivor is already \u003cb\u003eContaminated\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eTentacle Strike\u003c/b\u003e damages their health and increases \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eVaccine\u003c/b\u003e found in \u003cb\u003eSupply Cases\u003c/b\u003e cures \u003cb\u003eContamination\u003c/b\u003e. Their availability is limited. After using a \u003cb\u003eVaccine\u003c/b\u003e, the Survivor’s location is revealed by Killer Instinct.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eMutation Rate:\u003c/b\u003e Your power expands as your \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate\u003c/b\u003e grows. At \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate 2\u003c/b\u003e, hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it. At \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate 3\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eTentacle Strike\u003c/b\u003e’s range and movement speed increase when it\u0027s fully charged. The T-Virus icon displays the current \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ENEMY: Zombies\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf a \u003cb\u003ezombie\u003c/b\u003e hits a Survivor, they inflict them with the \u003cb\u003eContaminated\u003c/b\u003e effect. If already \u003cb\u003eContaminated\u003c/b\u003e, their health will be damaged.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eZombies\u003c/b\u003e can be destroyed by a \u003cb\u003eTentacle Strike\u003c/b\u003e to increase your \u003cb\u003eMutation Rate\u003c/b\u003e, and Survivors can destroy them with pallets. Destroyed \u003cb\u003ezombies\u003c/b\u003e eventually respawn.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b4/IconPowers_t-Virus.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thenightmare","name":"The Nightmare","bio":"A nightmare inducing Killer, passively forcing Survivors into his Dream World using his power, \u003cb\u003eDream Demon\u003c/b\u003e. It is here that Survivors become extremely vulnerable to his dream abilities. Using his \u003cb\u003eDream Projection\u003c/b\u003e ability he is able to quickly appear across the map and put pressure on Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eFire Up\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eRemember Me\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eBlood Warden\u003c/b\u003e, improve his abilities over time and make him stronger as the trial reaches its climax.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d5/K10_TheNightmare_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Blood Warden","description":"When an Exit Gate is opened, once per trial, when you hook a Survivor, both Exits are blocked for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see the Auras of Survivors within Exit Thresholds.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/eb/IconPerks_bloodWarden.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Fire Up","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou basic-break Pallets and Breakable Walls \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou damage Generators \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou pick-up and drop Survivors \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou basic-vault Windows \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5c/IconPerks_fireUp.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Remember Me","description":"Whenever the Obsession takes damage, you earn 1 Token, up to \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, Survivors who are not the Obsession open Exit Gates \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003e% slower.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/62/IconPerks_rememberMe.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Dream Demon","description":"All Survivors have a Sleep Meter that fills over time; once filled, Survivors fall asleep and enter the Dream World, where they are afflicted with the \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e status effect. Hitting an awake Survivor with a \u003ci\u003ebasic attack\u003c/i\u003e will also send them to the Dream World. Survivors can wake by failing Skill Checks, having an awake Survivor perform the \u003ci\u003eWake Up action\u003c/i\u003e, or using alarm clocks that also provide temporary immunity to sleep.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAwake Survivors hear \u003cb\u003eThe Nightmare\u003c/b\u003e\u0027s Terror Radius and see him within 16 meters, intermittently see him from 16 to 32 meters, and cannot see him beyond that.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: DREAM SNARES AND DREAM PALLETS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile selected, press the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge a \u003cb\u003eDream Snare\u003c/b\u003e, and press the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to release it. \u003cb\u003eDream Snares\u003c/b\u003e move quickly in a straight line, through walls but not over ledges. Survivors hit by the \u003cb\u003eDream Snare\u003c/b\u003e add time to their Sleep Meter if they are awake, while Sleeping Survivors will be \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e by \u003cb\u003e12%\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile selected, press the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to summon a \u003cb\u003eDream Pallet\u003c/b\u003e at a valid pallet location. Press the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e while targeting a \u003cb\u003eDream Pallet\u003c/b\u003e to rupture it. Survivors hit by the rupture add time to their Sleep Meter if awake, while sleeping Survivors will be injured.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: DREAM PROJECTION\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHold the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e to teleport to a generator or Survivor performing a healing action in the Dream World. Upon teleporting, all nearby Survivors add time to their Sleep Meter and are temporarily revealed with Killer Instinct. For each Survivor in the Dream World, the cooldown is reduced by \u003cb\u003e15%\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3a/IconPowers_dreamDemon.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thenurse","name":"The Nurse","bio":"A warping Killer, able to Blink through obstacles and quickly close gaps with her power, \u003cb\u003eSpencer\u0027s Last Breath\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eStridor\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eThanatophobia\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eA Nurse\u0027s Calling\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to decrease Survivor abilities and track them when they are injured.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/K04_TheNurse_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"A Nurse\u0027s Calling","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e28/30/32\u003c/b\u003em of Survivors who are healing or being healed, you see their Auras.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fe/IconPerks_aNursesCalling.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/20/A-Nurses-Calling.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Stridor","description":"Survivors\u0027 breathing noises are \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003e% louder and their Grunts of Pain are \u003cb\u003e30/40/50\u003c/b\u003e% louder.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/32/IconPerks_stridor.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Thanatophobia","description":"For each injured, downed, or hooked Survivor, all Survivors:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eCleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e1/1.5/2\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eRepair \u003cb\u003e1/1.5/2\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSabotage Hooks \u003cb\u003e1/1.5/2\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile 4 Survivors are either injured, downed or hooked, all above actions are additionally \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003e% slower.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a2/IconPerks_thanatophobia.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/61/Thanatophobia.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Spencer\u0027s Last Breath","description":"A powerful and violent last breath snatched from Crotus Prenn Asylum warden Patrick Spencer. Channelling its energy allows The Nurse to pierce and jump through the spirit world in a Blink multiple times in a row. Doing so leaves her in a state of fatigue.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGrants the Blink.Grants \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e additional Chain Blink.Attacks made after a Blink but before the ensuing fatigue are special attacks.After a Blink but before the ensuing fatigue, \u003cb\u003eThe Nurse\u003c/b\u003e can interrupt and grab Survivors.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6f/IconPowers_breath.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theoni","name":"The Oni","bio":"A monstrous Killer, able to absorb the blood energy of his injured foes, and then use that energy to transform into a brutal demon. Using his power, \u003cb\u003eYamaoka\u0027s Wrath\u003c/b\u003e, he can rush down Survivors at great speed and deal deadly strikes with his kanabō.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eZanshin Tactics\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBlood Echo\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eNemesis\u003c/b\u003e, provide navigational information, punish injured Survivors, and gain advantages over those that interfere.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/80/K18_TheOni_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Blood Echo","description":"Whenever you hook a Survivor, for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es, all injured Survivors:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eHemorrhage\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c3/IconPerks_bloodEcho.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Nemesis","description":"Whenever a Survivor blinds you, Locker-stuns or Pallet-stuns you, they become the Obsession.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor becomes the Obsession:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/33/IconPerks_nemesis.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Zanshin Tactics","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em, you see the Auras of Pallets and windows.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor drops a Pallet, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d3/IconPerks_zanshinTactics.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Yamaoka\u0027s Wrath","description":"The desire to destroy weaker bloodlines shaped into a literal force.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eYAMAOKA\u0027S WRATH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAbsorb Blood Orbs left by your injured foes. Press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to absorb Blood Orbs in the environment and fill your power gauge. When your power gauge is full, press and hold the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to initiate \u003cb\u003eBlood Fury\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eBlood Fury:\u003c/b\u003e While \u003cb\u003eBlood Fury\u003c/b\u003e is active, \u003cb\u003eThe Oni\u003c/b\u003e becomes lethal and gains access to additional abilities: \u003cb\u003eDemon Dash\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eDemon Strike\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Demon Dash\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e while \u003cb\u003eBlood Fury\u003c/b\u003e is active to perform a \u003cb\u003eDemon Dash\u003c/b\u003e. This ability allows \u003cb\u003eThe Oni\u003c/b\u003e to cover large distances at high speed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: Demon Strike\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e while \u003cb\u003eBlood Fury\u003c/b\u003e is active to perform a \u003cb\u003eDemon Strike\u003c/b\u003e in the direction you are facing. \u003cb\u003eDemon Strike\u003c/b\u003e has an extended lunge range and successful hits immediately put healthy Survivors into the dying state. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/86/IconPowers_yamaokasWrath_demon.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theonry","name":"The Onryō","bio":"A vengeful ghost imbued with the power of Nensha, the Onryō is able to silently and invisibly traverse the realm, manifesting when she is ready to strike.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eScourge Hook: Floods Of Rage\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCall Of Brine\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eMerciless Storm\u003c/b\u003e allow her to expose hidden Survivors, surveil generators, and hamper repair progress.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5f/K27_TheOnryo_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Call of Brine","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, it regresses \u003cb\u003e30/40/50\u003c/b\u003e% faster for \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor that time, whenever a Survivor hits a good basic Skill Check while repairing that Generator, you are alerted.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/IconPerks_callOfBrine.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6f/PerkAnimation_CallOfBrine.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Merciless Storm","description":"The first time each Generator has \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003e% progress: Survivors repairing it get special Skill Checks. If they miss one of these or stop repairing, that Generator is blocked for \u003cb\u003e16/18/20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/36/IconPerks_mercilessStorm.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/56/PerkAnimation_MercilessStorm_SurvivorPOV_CompletingAllSkillChecks.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Scourge Hook: Floods of Rage","description":"When the trial starts, 4 random Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor is unhooked from a Scourge Hook, you see the Auras of other Survivors for \u003cb\u003e5/6/7\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1c/IconPerks_scourgeHookFloodsOfRage.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Deluge of Fear","description":"Through the medium of a mysterious videotape, Sadako spreads her curse to unwitting viewers and causes their untimely deaths.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: MANIFESTATION\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBefore Manifesting, The Onryo becomes \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e and invisible to Survivors, but intermittently visible when within \u003cb\u003e24 meters\u003c/b\u003e of them. The Onryo must Manifest to attack Survivors. Press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to \u003cb\u003eManifest\u003c/b\u003e in your current position. Briefly after \u003cb\u003eManifesting\u003c/b\u003e, The Onryo will continue to be intermittently visible to Survivors when within \u003cb\u003e24 meters\u003c/b\u003e. Afterward, she will be fully visible within \u003cb\u003e24 meters\u003c/b\u003e for as long as she remains \u003cb\u003eManifested\u003c/b\u003e. The Onryo can \u003cb\u003eDemanifest\u003c/b\u003e by pressing and holding the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: PROJECTION\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Onryo can also take material form by \u003cb\u003eProjecting\u003c/b\u003e herself through a TV. Press the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e while looking at a powered TV to \u003cb\u003eProject\u003c/b\u003e into it, shutting the TV off in the process.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSURVIVOR AFFLICTION: CONDEMNED\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors can temporarily turn off TVs with the \u003cb\u003eRetrieve Tape\u003c/b\u003e action. At the TV furthest from their position, Survivors can spread The Onryo\u0027s message by inserting their Tape, which reduces their \u003cb\u003eCondemned\u003c/b\u003e progress; this also turns the TV off.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the power meter is full and The Onryo \u003cb\u003eProjects\u003c/b\u003e, any Survivor near a powered TV will gain \u003cb\u003eCondemned\u003c/b\u003e progress.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHooking a Survivor affected by \u003cb\u003eCondemned\u003c/b\u003e locks in 3 of their stacks, making it impossible to remove them for the rest of the trial.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA fully \u003cb\u003eCondemned\u003c/b\u003e Survivor is revealed by \u003cb\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/b\u003e and can be killed once downed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4c/IconPowers_delugeOfFear2.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thepig","name":"The Pig","bio":"A tormenting Killer, able to Crouch into stealth mode, then Ambush Survivors from a short distance. She can also apply \u003cb\u003eReverse Bear Traps\u003c/b\u003e to downed Survivors, forcing them to remove it before the timer runs out. If the timer expires, they die instantly.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHangman\u0027s Trick\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSurveillance\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eMake Your Choice\u003c/b\u003e, give her more map control and expose altruistic Survivors.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5c/K11_ThePig_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Make your Choice","description":"Whenever a Survivor unhooks another or themselves while you are at least \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em away:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey scream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6b/IconPerks_makeYourChoice.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Scourge Hook: Hangman\u0027s Trick","description":"When the trial starts, 4 random Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile carrying a Survivor, you see the Auras of Survivors within \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003em of Scourge Hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor starts sabotaging a Hook, you are alerted.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9a/IconPerks_scourgeHookHangmansTrick.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/44/HangmansTrick.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Surveillance","description":"You see the Auras of regressing Generators.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Generator stops regressing, you see its Aura for \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGenerator repair noises can be heard from \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003em farther away.\u003cbr\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/eb/IconPerks_surveillance.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/55/Surveillance.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Jigsaw\u0027s Baptism","description":"Forever devoted to her master\u0027s cause, she punishes the ungrateful and the guilty with slyness and murderous puzzles. \u003cb\u003eThe Pig\u003c/b\u003e can move stealthily, dash in Ambush attacks and put deadly Reverse Bear Traps on Survivors\u0027 heads.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eJIGSAW\u0027S BAPTISM\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eStart the trial with \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e \u003ci\u003einactive\u003c/i\u003e Reverse Bear Traps. While standing over a Survivor in the dying state, press the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to place an \u003ci\u003einactive\u003c/i\u003e Reverse Bear Trap on The Survivor. Reverse Bear Traps become \u003ci\u003eactive\u003c/i\u003e when any generator in the trial is completed. Survivors may attempt to free themselves from \u003ci\u003eactive\u003c/i\u003e or \u003ci\u003einactive\u003c/i\u003e Reverse Bear Traps by searching Jigsaw Boxes located in the environment to find the correct key.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eActive Reverse Bear Traps:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen Reverse Bear Traps become \u003ci\u003eactive\u003c/i\u003e, they initiate a countdown timer. A Survivor with an \u003ci\u003eactive\u003c/i\u003e Reverse Bear Trap is automatically sacrificed when their timer expires or if they attempt to leave the trial with an \u003ci\u003eactive\u003c/i\u003e Reverse Bear Trap still attached.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: CROUCH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e to Crouch. Press the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability button\u003c/i\u003e again while Crouched to stand. \u003cb\u003eThe Pig\u003c/b\u003e moves at a slower speed while Crouched. \u003cb\u003eThe Pig\u003c/b\u003e is granted the \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e status effect while Crouched.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: AMBUSH\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e while Crouched to dash and perform an \u003cb\u003eAmbush\u003c/b\u003e attack.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b0/IconPowers_jigsawsBaptism.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theplague","name":"The Plague","bio":"A devout Killer, able to infect Survivors from a short distance using her power, \u003cb\u003eVile Purge\u003c/b\u003e. Survivors inflicted by this contamination risk becoming injured or broken, unless they find a way to cure themselves in a Pool of Devotion.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eCorrupt Intervention\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eInfectious Fright\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eDark Devotion\u003c/b\u003e, give her the ability to hinder Survivor objectives, while simultaneously confusing and frightening those within her presence.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fe/K15_ThePlague_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Corrupt Intervention","description":"When the trial starts, the \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e farthest Generators from you are blocked for \u003cb\u003e80/100/120\u003c/b\u003es, or until you down a Survivor.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/10/IconPerks_corruptIntervention.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Dark Devotion","description":"Whenever the Obsession takes damage, for \u003cb\u003e35/40/45\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Terror Radius is set to \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003em.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Obsession has your Terror Radius.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4f/IconPerks_darkDevotion.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Infectious Fright","description":"Whenever a Survivor is downed, Survivors within your Terror Radius scream and you are alerted for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6d/IconPerks_infectiousFright.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Vile Purge","description":"Her condition deteriorated as the plague overtook her body: her toes blackened, her neck mushroomed into cysts, and her throat gagged with bloody vomit.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eVILE PURGE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eInfect environmental objects and Survivors with \u003cb\u003eVile Purge\u003c/b\u003e to create an unending cycle of sickness. Press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to charge \u003cb\u003eVile Purge\u003c/b\u003e, and release the button to unleash a stream of infectious bile. Hitting a Survivor will cause them to become infected. Hitting an environmental object will cause it to become infected for a short time. Survivors interacting with infected objects will also become infected.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen a Survivor\u0027s infection indicator is completely filled, The Survivor is put into the injured state, is afflicted by the \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e status effect, and forced to vomit at random intervals.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: INGEST CORRUPTION\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eInfected Survivors can heal themselves to full health and cure their infection by cleansing at a \u003ci\u003ePool of Devotion\u003c/i\u003e. This action corrupts the pool, allowing \u003cb\u003eThe Plague\u003c/b\u003e to consume the corruption and empower her purge. Press and hold the \u003ci\u003eInteraction button\u003c/i\u003e while next to a corrupt \u003ci\u003ePool of Devotion\u003c/i\u003e to transform \u003cb\u003eVile Purge\u003c/b\u003e into \u003cb\u003eCorrupt Purge\u003c/b\u003e. This action removes the corruption from the pool.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: CORRUPT PURGE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter using the \u003cb\u003eIngest Corruption\u003c/b\u003e ability, \u003cb\u003eVile Purge\u003c/b\u003e is replaced by \u003cb\u003eCorrupt Purge\u003c/b\u003e for a short duration. \u003cb\u003eCorrupt Purge\u003c/b\u003e instantly damages any Survivor hit by its stream, however, it no longer applies infection to Survivors or environmental objects.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fd/IconPowers_vilePurge.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theshape","name":"The Shape","bio":"A haunting Killer who stalks Survivors to feed his power.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eSave the Best for Last\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003ePlay with your Food\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eDying Light\u003c/b\u003e select one Survivor to become the Obsession and trigger deadly effects based on the Obsession\u0027s status.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b5/K05_TheShape_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dying Light","description":"Whenever you hook a Survivor that is not the Obsession, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile the Obsession is alive, for each Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eOther Survivors heal \u003cb\u003e2/2.5/3\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOther Survivors repair \u003cb\u003e2/2.5/3\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOther Survivors sabotage Hooks \u003cb\u003e2/2.5/3\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Obsession:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eHeals other Survivors \u003cb\u003e33\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUnhooks other Survivors \u003cb\u003e33\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/48/IconPerks_dyingLight.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Play With Your Food","description":"Whenever you stop chasing the Obsession, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, gain \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you attack, lose \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/18/IconPerks_playWithYourFood.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Save the best for last","description":"Whenever you damage a Survivor who is not the Obsession with a basic-attack, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, your basic-attack cooldown are \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% shorter.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever the Obsession takes damage, lose \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e Tokens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile the Obsession is dead, you cannot earn Tokens.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6a/IconPerks_saveTheBestForLast.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Evil Within","description":"The Shape stalks his prey, adapting to the pursuit, waiting for the perfect moment to unleash evil.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Shape can switch between three modes of hunting his prey. Each mode has different strengths and weaknesses.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL MODE: STALKER\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Shape moves slowly and is \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e. In \u003cb\u003eStalker mode\u003c/b\u003e, press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower\u003c/i\u003e button to \u003cb\u003eStalk\u003c/b\u003e a nearby Survivor and fill the \u003cb\u003eStalk Meter\u003c/b\u003e. When the \u003cb\u003eStalk Meter\u003c/b\u003e is full, \u003cb\u003eEvil Incarnate mode\u003c/b\u003e is unlocked.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL MODE: PURSUER\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Shape moves quickly and has a \u003cb\u003e16 meter\u003c/b\u003e Terror Radius. Vault, basic-break, lunge, and stun recovery speeds are increased.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL MODE: EVIL INCARNATE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Shape’s Terror Radius is increased to \u003cb\u003e32 meters\u003c/b\u003e. Vault, basic-break, and stun recovery speeds are increased. Survivors who have reached the second hook stage can be killed.\u003cb\u003eEvil Incarnate mode\u003c/b\u003e ends after \u003cb\u003e60 seconds\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: SLAUGHTERING STRIKE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn \u003cb\u003eEvil Incarnate mode\u003c/b\u003e, hold the \u003ci\u003ePower\u003c/i\u003e button to charge \u003cb\u003eSlaughtering Strike\u003c/b\u003e and press the \u003ci\u003eAttack\u003c/i\u003e button to unleash it. The longer the \u003ci\u003ePower\u003c/i\u003e button is held, the more distance on the attack. Survivors hit by \u003cb\u003eSlaughtering Strike\u003c/b\u003e are downed, even if healthy. Hitting a dropped pallet or breakable wall will special-break it.","icon":null}},{"id":"thesingularity","name":"The Singularity","bio":"The Singularity is a relentless Killer, able to launch Biopods to move quickly across the map.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eGenetic Limits\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eForced Hesitation\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eMachine Learning\u003c/b\u003e allow him to Exhaust newly injured Survivors, Hinder anyone close to a Survivor put in the dying state, and compromise generators.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/24/K32_TheSingularity_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Forced Hesitation","description":"Whenever you down a Survivor, other Survivors within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em of the downed Survivor gain \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4c/IconPerks_forcedHesitation.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Genetic Limits","description":"Whenever a Survivor takes damage, they gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6d/IconPerks_geneticLimits.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Machine Learning","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, it becomes compromised.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen that Generator is completed by Survivors:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOnly one Generator can be compromised at a time.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/01/IconPerks_machineLearning.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/50/PerkAnimation_SelfAware_ScratchMarks.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Quantum Instantiation","description":"A dark crystalline structure in an ancient ruin gifted—or perhaps cursed—Hux with sentience. He built a new body, and with it, a terrifying way to bend the rules of physics to his benefit.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Singularity can shoot and spawn Biopods around the map; these Biopods can attach to any vertical surface they land on. The Singularity can control a Biopod remotely and look through it, and tag Survivors, afflicting them with a Temporal Slipstream. When Slipstreamed, The Singularity can teleport next to the Slipstreamed Survivor either by using the Biopods to tag them, or by shooting them. When a Slipstreamed Survivor is in proximity to another Survivor, the Slipstream can spread. All Slipstreamed Survivors are briefly revealed with Killer Instinct.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL STATE: OVERCLOCK MODE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter a successful Slipstream teleport, The Singularity enters Overclock Mode. In this state, The Singularity gains \u003cb\u003e3%\u003c/b\u003e movement speed for \u003cb\u003e5.7 seconds\u003c/b\u003e, can basic-break dropped pallets or breakable walls and basic-vault windows faster, and cannot be stunned. Attempts to stun remove Overclock Mode and The Singularity is afflicted with \u003cb\u003e50% Hindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3 seconds\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL INTERACTION: ELECTROMAGNETIC PULSE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAt the beginning of each Trial, several Supply Cases spawn, each containing an EMP. Survivors can use these EMPs to remove the Slipstream from themselves or others, or to briefly disable a Biopod. Once used, the EMP is destroy","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/df/IconPowers_quantumInstantiation.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theskullmerchant","name":"The Skull Merchant","bio":"The Skull Merchant is a tactical Killer, able to place Drones that detect and debilitate her targets.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eGame Afoot\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eTHWACK!\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eLeverage\u003c/b\u003e allow her to gain Haste from pursuing your Obsession, force screams from Survivors when breaking walls or pallets, and reduce Survivors\u0027 heal speed the more times you place them on hooks.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/64/K31_TheSkullMerchant_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Game Afoot","description":"While chasing the Obsession, whenever you basic-break Pallets or Breakable Walls, or damage Generators, you gain \u003cb\u003e7\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you damage the Survivor with the most chase time with a basic-attack, they become the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/53/IconPerks_gameAfoot.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f5/PerkAnimation_GameAfoot_Haste.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Leverage","description":"Whenever a Survivor unhooks another or themselves, they heal \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% slower for \u003cb\u003e60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c6/IconPerks_leverage.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"THWACK!","description":"When the trial starts, you earn \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, up to \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you hook a Survivor, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you break a Pallet or Breakable Wall, spend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token. Then, all Survivors within \u003cb\u003e36\u003c/b\u003em scream and you see their Auras for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bb/IconPerks_thwack.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/df/PerkAnimation_Thwack.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Eyes In The Sky","description":"\u003ci\u003eInspired by the dark mangas created by her father, The Skull Merchant relentlessly hunts her prey using the latest in surveillance technology.\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Skull Merchant begins the match with six Drones. Press the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to deploy a Drone. Recalling a Drone grants \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for 8 seconds. Once detected by a scan line, a Survivor gains scan immunity and cannot be detected by other scan lines for a few seconds.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors can attempt to hack Drones. Failure partially fills their \u003cb\u003eLock On\u003c/b\u003e meter; Success disables the Drone for 45 seconds.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: RADAR\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eAbility Button\u003c/i\u003e to open a Radar to see the locations of Survivors detected by Drones and those with \u003cb\u003eClaw Traps\u003c/b\u003e. The Radar can be used to change a Drone\u0027s rotation direction or to recall a Drone.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen a Survivor is detected by a Drone shortly after its deployment or change in rotation, The Skull Merchant gains \u003cb\u003e5% Haste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e8 seconds\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL EFFECT: LOCK ON\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe \u003cb\u003eLock On\u003c/b\u003e meter fills when scanned by a Drone and when failing to disable a Drone. When the meter is full, the Survivor receives a \u003cb\u003eClaw Trap\u003c/b\u003e, becomes Injured, and suffers from the \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e status effect. Additional scans briefly apply a 10% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e status effect.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA \u003cb\u003eClaw Trap\u003c/b\u003e broadcasts the Survivor’s location to the Killer and is only removed when its battery dies.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c6/IconPowers_eyesInTheSky.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theslasher","name":"The Slasher","bio":"The Slasher is the embodiment of horror, a relentless Killer who is always on the hunt.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHex: Scared to Death\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSilent Shadow\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eRampage\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to excel at chases, stealthily hunt Survivors, and recover after being stunned.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"Hex: Scared to Death","description":"After you hook \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e different Survivors, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile chasing a Survivor, whenever you basic-break a Pallet, Survivors within \u003cb\u003e11/12/13\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eScream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003e11/12/13\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Rampage","description":"Whenever you basic-break a Pallet or Breakable Wall, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e13\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you are blinded or Pallet-stunned, for the next \u003cb\u003e13\u003c/b\u003es you gain \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for each Token. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e30/25/20\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Silent Shadow","description":"Whenever you hook a Survivor, you gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e11/12/13\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all Generators are completed, you gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":null,"video":null}],"power":{"name":"Omnipresent Evil","description":"\u003cb\u003ePOWER: Omnipresent Evil\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eActive Ability\u003c/i\u003e button to activate \u003cb\u003eOmnipresent Evil\u003c/b\u003e. The Slasher becomes invisible and gains \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e, but cannot see Survivors or their Scratch Marks. \u003cb\u003eMist Clouds\u003c/b\u003e reveal the location of Survivors who are not moving. \u003cb\u003eFootprints\u003c/b\u003e reveal the path of Survivors who are walking or running.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eOmnipresent Evil\u003c/b\u003e is deactivated by using \u003cb\u003eJump Scare\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Jump Scare\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile \u003cb\u003eOmnipresent Evil\u003c/b\u003e is activated, look at a Pallet, Breakable Wall, or Window to quickly move to it and perform a special-break or special-vault action. The \u003ci\u003eSecondary Action\u003c/i\u003e button switches the side you will face when performing \u003cb\u003eJump Scare\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eJump Scare\u003c/b\u003e exits \u003cb\u003eOmnipresent Evil\u003c/b\u003e mode, temporarily grants \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e, and reveals detected Survivors with \u003cb\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/b\u003e. Haste is removed if The Slasher directly downs a Survivor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: Throwing Spikes\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGrab a \u003cb\u003eSpike\u003c/b\u003e from \u003cb\u003eScrap Piles\u003c/b\u003e or \u003cb\u003eHooks\u003c/b\u003e. Hold the \u003ci\u003eSecondary Action\u003c/i\u003e button to ready the \u003cb\u003eSpike\u003c/b\u003e and tap the \u003ci\u003eAttack\u003c/i\u003e button to throw. \u003cb\u003eSpikes\u003c/b\u003e are replenished throughout the map when \u003cb\u003eOmnipresent Evil\u003c/b\u003e is activated.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eA \u003cb\u003eSpike\u003c/b\u003e knocks back a Survivor and damages them for one health state.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors will be \u003cb\u003eImpaled\u003c/b\u003e if they are hit with a \u003cb\u003eHook Spike\u003c/b\u003e. They cannot heal past the injured state and the embedded \u003cb\u003eHook Spike\u003c/b\u003e will have an Aura visible to the Killer.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eInjured Survivors will be both \u003cb\u003eImpaled\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eImmobilized\u003c/b\u003e if they are hit with a \u003cb\u003eSpike\u003c/b\u003e and knocked into a wall.","icon":null}},{"id":"thespirit","name":"The Spirit","bio":"A phase-walking Killer, able to catch Survivors off-guard with her traversal power, \u003cb\u003eYamaoka’s Haunting\u003c/b\u003e. Her power allows her to Teleport from one place to another without being seen.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eSpirit Fury\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Haunted Ground\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eRancor\u003c/b\u003e, give her tools to observe and bait Survivors, and deal with obstacles directly in her path.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f1/K13_TheSpirit_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Hex: Haunted Ground","description":"When the trial starts, 2 Dull Totems ignite.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen either of those Hex Totems is blessed or cleansed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAll Survivors gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe other Totem is extinguished.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c4/IconPerks_hexHauntedGround.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Rancor","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou are alerted to the position of all Survivors for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Obsession sees your Aura for \u003cb\u003e5/4/3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all Generators are completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Obsession gains \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou can Kill the Obsession.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a2/IconPerks_rancor.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Spirit Fury","description":"After you break \u003cb\u003e4/3/2\u003c/b\u003e Pallets, when you are Pallet-stunned, the Pallet is destroyed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a6/IconPerks_spiritFury.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7f/SpiritFury.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Yamaoka’s Haunting","description":"The Spirit can use her power, Yamaoka’s Haunting, to enter an ethereal plane and reappear at a new location.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTap and Hold the Power button to charge. The Spirit will depart her physical body, leaving behind a stationary \u0027husk\u0027.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile Yamaoka’s Haunting is active:The Spirit may traverse freely to a new location, moving at a faster rate for a short duration. She is still confined to movement within the physical environments and surroundings.The Spirit leaves the physical plane, losing sight of all Survivors. She can, however, still sense the scratch marks they leave in the environment.The Spirit will produce an audible cue at her current location.Once the power has ended, The Spirit retains her speed boost for a brief period and her husk fades away.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eUsing Yamaoka’s Haunting depletes The Spirit\u0027s power bar. The power bar will automatically replenish over time. The power bar must be fully replenished before it can be triggered again.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bb/IconPowers_yamaokasHaunting.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thetrapper","name":"The Trapper","bio":"An area-control Killer, able to apply pressure across the map by placing deadly \u003cb\u003eBear Traps\u003c/b\u003e for Survivors to step in.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eUnnerving Presence\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBrutal Strength\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eAgitation\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to chase and carry Survivors more effectively.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/81/K01_TheTrapper_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Agitation","description":"While carrying a Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e6/12/18\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Terror Radius is \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003em larger.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ac/IconPerks_agitation.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Brutal Strength","description":"You basic-break Pallets and Breakable Walls, and damage Generators \u003cb\u003e10/15/20\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3d/IconPerks_brutalStrength.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5e/BrutalStrength_pre170.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Unnerving Presence","description":"Survivors within your Terror Radius get \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e% more basic Skill Checks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe good zone of basic Skill Checks is \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003e% smaller.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a4/IconPerks_unnervingPresence.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8e/SO_UP_Tech.mp4/revision/latest"}],"power":{"name":"Bear Trap","description":"A large foothold trap made of steel. Traps are found lying around the area waiting to be picked up and set anywhere.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eBEAR TRAP\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBy default, you start the trial with \u003cb\u003e2 Bear Traps\u003c/b\u003e. Find and collect more throughout the environment.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSet Bear Trap:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to set a \u003cb\u003eBear Trap\u003c/b\u003e on a valid location in front of you. A set \u003cb\u003eBear Trap\u003c/b\u003e will immobilize and incapacitate any player that steps on it. A healthy Survivor that steps in a set \u003cb\u003eBear Trap\u003c/b\u003e will also become injured but may attempt to escape the trap. Press the \u003ci\u003eInteraction button\u003c/i\u003e to pick-up a nearby Survivor who is Incapacitated by a \u003cb\u003eBear Trap\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eReset Trap:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e while standing near a \u003cb\u003eBear Trap\u003c/b\u003e in the environment to reset it where it lies, if it is not already set.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSetting and resetting Bear Traps grants The Trapper \u003cb\u003e7.5% Haste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e5 seconds\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eCollect Bear Trap:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the \u003ci\u003eInteraction button\u003c/i\u003e while standing near a \u003cb\u003eBear Trap\u003c/b\u003e in the environment to collect it. By default, you may carry a maximum of \u003cb\u003e2 Bear Traps\u003c/b\u003e at any time.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0f/IconPowers_trap.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thetrickster","name":"The Trickster","bio":"A ranged Killer, able to quickly unleash a flurry of blades by using his power, \u003cb\u003eShowstopper\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eStarstruck\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eHex: Crowd Control\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eNo Way Out\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to quickly down would-be rescuers and block areas of the environment to his advantage.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c9/K23_TheTrickster_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Hex: Crowd Control","description":"The first time a Survivor medium or fast-vaults a Window, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe last \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003e Windows Survivors medium or fast-vault are blocked.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou basic-vault blocked Windows \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see the Auras of blocked Windows within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f1/IconPerks_hexCrowdControl.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"No Way Out","description":"The first time you Hook each Survivor, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all Generators are completed, when a Survivor starts opening an Exit Gate:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eIt is blocked \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003es, plus \u003cb\u003e6/9/12\u003c/b\u003es for each Token.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou are alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bb/IconPerks_noWayOut.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5d/PerkAnimation_NoWayOut.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Starstruck","description":"While carrying a Survivor, Survivors within your Terror Radius gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e. This ends \u003cb\u003e26/28/30\u003c/b\u003es after:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey leave your Terror Radius.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou drop or Hook the carried Survivor.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6e/IconPerks_starstruck.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Showstopper","description":"\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: BLADE THROW\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the Power button to enter the Throw State. Tap the Attack button to throw a single Blade, or hold down to unleash a flurry of Blades. Restock Blades at Lockers.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL EFFECT: LACERATION\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors\u0027 Laceration Meter increases when hit by Blades. When the meter is filled, they lose a health state. Laceration decreases after a delay if Survivors are not hit by Blades. Injuring Survivors with basic attacks decreases Laceration.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: STYLE POINTS \u0026 STYLE RANKS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBy throwing Blades, injuring Survivors and performing distinct actions back-to-back, The Trickster earns Style Points. Regular actions give few Style Points, while skillful actions give more.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEarning Style Points causes The Trickster to go up in Style Ranks. Each Style Rank improves his Blade throw and restocking speed. Earning Style Points refreshes the current Style Rank timer.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL CONDITION/ABILITY: S-RANK \u0026 MAIN EVENT\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAt S-Rank, The Trickster gains a \u003cb\u003e44-meter\u003c/b\u003e Terror radius, the Lullaby is disabled, Laceration Meters decay blocked, Blade throw and restock speeds increase further, and he can trigger Main Event.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eMain Event is activated by pressing the Ability button, causing The Trickster to throw unlimited Blades at high speed. Each Blade hitting Survivors awards bonus Style Points. End Main Event early by pressing the Ability button. Main Event ending triggers fatigue.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eMain Event cannot be activated near hooked Survivors.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fb/IconPowers_showstopper.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thetwins","name":"The Twins","bio":"A cooperative pair of Killers, able to divide and hunt together using their power, \u003cb\u003eBlood Bond\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTheir personal perks, \u003cb\u003eHoarder\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eOppression\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eCoup de Grâce\u003c/b\u003e allow them to monitor Survivors’ actions, impede their progress, and hunt more effectively.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/17/K22_TheTwins_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Coup de Grâce","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, you earn \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, up to \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you lunge-attack, spend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token to make it \u003cb\u003e70/75/80\u003c/b\u003e% longer.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bd/IconPerks_coupDeGr%C3%A2ce.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hoarder","description":"When the trial starts, \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e more Chests appear.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor picks-up an Item or starts unlocking a Chest within \u003cb\u003e32/48/64\u003c/b\u003em of you, you are alerted.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/23/IconPerks_hoarder.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Oppression","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator, up to \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e other Generators start regressing. Survivors repairing them get a special Skill Check. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e45/40/35\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a1/IconPerks_oppression.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Blood Bond","description":"Though forever bound through blood \u0026 trauma, The Twins have been granted the power to separate from their shared body. Together they hunt as brother and sister, doubling the threat to Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eBlood Bond\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to unleash \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e. Swap control between \u003cb\u003eCharlotte\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e by tapping the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile left on his own, \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e will trigger \u003cb\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/b\u003e, revealing to \u003cb\u003eCharlotte\u003c/b\u003e the outlines of Survivors who are walking or running near him. Survivors who can hear \u003cb\u003eVictor’s\u003c/b\u003e shrieks are susceptible. However, \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e can be crushed by Survivors while \u003cb\u003eCharlotte\u003c/b\u003e is being controlled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf crushed, \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e will re-grow on \u003cb\u003eCharlotte\u003c/b\u003e after some time has passed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ATTACK: Pounce\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile controlling \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e, hold the \u003ci\u003eAbility button\u003c/i\u003e to charge a \u003cb\u003ePounce\u003c/b\u003e and tap the \u003ci\u003eAttack button\u003c/i\u003e to unleash it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSuccessfully landing a \u003cb\u003ePounce\u003c/b\u003e deals damage to the Survivor. If the Survivor was at full health, \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e will latch on, triggering \u003cb\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/b\u003e and revealing the location of all nearby Survivors. While latched on, the Survivor will be afflicted with the \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eIncapacitated\u003c/b\u003e status effects. They will be unable to enter lockers or leave through the exit gate. The Survivor can crush \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e while he\u0027s latched onto them by completing the \u003cb\u003eRemove\u003c/b\u003e action.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf \u003cb\u003eVictor\u003c/b\u003e misses his \u003cb\u003ePounce\u003c/b\u003e, he is momentarily vulnerable and can be crushed by a Survivor. If Victor lands on an obstacle taller than himself, he will be destroyed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/28/IconPowers_bloodBond.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"theunknown","name":"The Unknown","bio":"A being beyond understanding, though many have tried.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIts personal perks, \u003cb\u003eUnbound\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eUnforeseen\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eUndone\u003c/b\u003e allow it to move quicker, put its Terror Radius on a generator, and deplete generator progress.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/51/K35_TheUnknown_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Unbound","description":"Whenever a healthy Survivor becomes injured, for the next \u003cb\u003e24/27/30\u003c/b\u003es, whenever you basic-vault a window, gain \u003cb\u003e7\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/91/IconPerks_unbound.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Undone","description":"Whenever a Survivor misses a basic Skill Check, earn \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, up to \u003cb\u003e18/24/30\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you damage a Generator, spend all Tokens. For each Token spent:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Generator loses \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e% progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Generator is blocked for \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen that Generator is unblocked, it begins regressing. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/11/IconPerks_undone.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Unforeseen","description":"Whenever you damage a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Terror Radius is set to that Generator for \u003cb\u003e22/26/30\u003c/b\u003es and its radius is \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e for that time.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0c/IconPerks_unforeseen.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"UVX","description":"Some believed a specimen was recovered by the military for their experiments. The codename: Unknown Venom X.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress the Power button to charge \u003cb\u003eUVX\u003c/b\u003e. Once ready, press the Attack button to launch \u003cb\u003eUVX\u003c/b\u003e, a bouncing Projectile which creates a Blast Area upon impact. Survivors become \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e by \u003cb\u003e6%\u003c/b\u003e if touched by \u003cb\u003eUVX\u003c/b\u003e while airborne.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors touching the Blast Area become \u003cb\u003eWeakened\u003c/b\u003e. \u003cb\u003eWeakened\u003c/b\u003e Survivors lose health states if touched by Blast Areas. Survivors lose \u003cb\u003eWeakened\u003c/b\u003e by successfully Staring Down The Unknown.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: HALLUCINATIONS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Unknown will intermittently create up to 4 \u003cb\u003eHallucinations\u003c/b\u003e. \u003cb\u003eHallucinations\u003c/b\u003e cannot be created while charging \u003cb\u003eUVX\u003c/b\u003e, performing interactions, or in proximity to map objects like hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever Survivors are touched by Blast Areas or otherwise become \u003cb\u003eWeakened\u003c/b\u003e, the next \u003cb\u003eHallucination\u0027s\u003c/b\u003e spawn time decreases by 10 seconds.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Unknown can Teleport to \u003cb\u003eHallucinations\u003c/b\u003e, leaving behind a temporary Decoy. Survivors can remove \u003cb\u003eHallucinations\u003c/b\u003e from the trial with the Dispel ability. \u003cb\u003eWeakened\u003c/b\u003e Survivors take longer to Dispel. If Dispel is not completed, Survivors become \u003cb\u003eWeakened\u003c/b\u003e and trigger \u003cb\u003eKiller Instinct\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e“... Request for analysis [REDACTED] incident [REDACTED] awaiting approval.” - Excerpt from leaked OSS report","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e8/IconPowers_ChargeUVX_K35.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thewraith","name":"The Wraith","bio":"A stealth Killer, able to Cloak and Uncloak at the ringing of his \u003cb\u003eWailing Bell\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003ePredator\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBloodhound\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eShadowborn\u003c/b\u003e, give him extra abilities to track and locate Survivors, making him a very efficient hunter.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c2/K02_TheWraith_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Bloodhound","description":"Pools of Blood are brighter and last \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003es longer.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e0/IconPerks_bloodhound.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/07/Bloodhound.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Predator","description":"When you stop chasing a Survivor, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/73/IconPerks_predator.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Shadowborn","description":"Whenever you are blinded, gain \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ac/IconPerks_shadowborn.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Wailing Bell","description":"A heavy cast iron bell imbued with ancient powers. Allows its user to enter and walk the spirit world when rung.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eWAILING BELL\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePress and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e to \u003cb\u003eCloak\u003c/b\u003e. Press and hold the \u003ci\u003ePower button\u003c/i\u003e again while Cloaked to \u003cb\u003eUncloak\u003c/b\u003e, granting a \u003cb\u003e1 second\u003c/b\u003e burst of speed upon reappearing. The Wailing Bell can be heard up to a distance of \u003cb\u003e24 meters\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eCloak:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile Cloaked, \u003cb\u003eThe Wraith\u003c/b\u003e is granted increased movement speed, near total invisibility, and the \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e status effect. \u003cb\u003eThe Wraith\u003c/b\u003e may not attack while Cloaked, but can interact with environmental objects.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f4/IconPowers_bell.png/revision/latest"}},{"id":"thexenomorph","name":"The Xenomorph","bio":"A relentless specimen from a distant planet, The Xenomorph is vicious, agile, and cunning.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIts personal perks, \u003cb\u003eUltimate Weapon\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eRapid Brutality\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eAlien Instinct\u003c/b\u003e allow it to cause nearby Survivors to scream, gain Haste after basic attacks, and see auras of faraway Survivors.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/64/K33_TheXenomorph_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Alien Instinct","description":"Whenever you hook a Survivor, the farthest injured Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eGains \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/34/IconPerks_alienInstinct.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Rapid Brutality","description":"Whenever you damage a Survivor with a basic-attack, you gain \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile chasing a Survivor, you cannot gain Bloodlust.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d4/IconPerks_rapidBrutality.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Ultimate Weapon","description":"Whenever you search a Locker, Survivors within \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eBlindness\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eScream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e55/50/45\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8a/IconPerks_ultimateWeapon.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"power":{"name":"Hidden Pursuit","description":"Supposedly responding to a distress signal, the Nostromo\u0027s crew landed on LV-426. What they found there became one of humanity\u0027s greatest horrors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen The Xenomorph is in a trial, a series of tunnels become available to it. By accessing a Control Station, it can enter these tunnels to quickly move around the map, detect the presence of nearby Survivors, and speed up the cooldown time of its Crawler Mode. Exiting a Control Station momentarily deactivates deployed Turrets and tags nearby Survivors with Killer Instinct.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ABILITY: CRAWLER MODE\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Xenomorph enters Crawler Mode automatically when not on cooldown. In Crawler Mode, The Xenomorph walks on four legs and becomes stealthier, reducing its Terror Radius. While in Crawler Mode, The Xenomorph also has access to a brutal Tail Attack.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL MAP FEATURE: CONTROL STATIONS\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSeven Control Stations are scattered across the map. Survivors can interact with these stations to get a Remote Flame Turret, while The Xenomorph can enter and exit the tunnels underneath the Control Stations.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003eSPECIAL ITEM: REMOTE FLAME TURRET\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTurrets can be placed in the map to counteract The Xenomorph. When The Xenomorph enters the radius and line of sight of a Turret, the Turret attacks; this attack staggers The Xenomorph and can cause Crawler Mode to end. If a Turret successfully knocks The Xenomorph out of Crawler Mode or fires for too long, it overheats, and must be repaired by a Survivor. The Xenomorph can attack Turrets to destroy them. Carrying a Turret makes you immune to detection while the killer is in the tunnel.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e“Its structural perfection is matched only by its hostility.” – Ash, Science Officer","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b7/IconPowers_hiddenPursuit.png/revision/latest"}}],"survivors":[{"id":"acevisconti","name":"Ace Visconti","bio":"A lucky gambler, improving the odds of the entire team.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eOpen Handed\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eUp the Ante\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eAce in the Hole\u003c/b\u003e, boost the Luck of all Survivors and help with unlocking chests.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b9/S07_AceVisconti_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Ace in the Hole","description":"Whenever you loot an item from a Chest, it will have:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eA Visceral or lower rarity add-on.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003e50/75/100\u003c/b\u003e% chance for an Uncommon or lower rarity add-on.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you escape, you keep your add-ons.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/24/IconPerks_aceInTheHole.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cf/PerkAnimation_AceInTheHole.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Open-Handed","description":"All Survivors see Auras that have a range from \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003em farther.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5d/IconPerks_open-Handed.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Up the Ante","description":"For each other Survivor alive, all Survivors are \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003e% luckier.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAll Survivors can attempt to unhook themselves.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a3/IconPerks_upTheAnte.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"adawong","name":"Ada Wong","bio":"Ada Wong is a mysterious secret agent whose skill in espionage makes her a dangerous foe.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eWiretap\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eReactive Healing\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eLow Profile\u003c/b\u003e allow her to spy on a Killer, gain a surge of healing when her allies are hurt, and leave no trace when she is the final Survivor.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5e/S32_AdaWong_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Low Profile","description":"When all other Survivors are downed or hooked, for \u003cb\u003e70/80/90\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou make no Grunts of Pain.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fb/IconPerks_lowProfile.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Reactive Healing","description":"While injured, whenever another Survivor within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em of you takes damage, you gain \u003cb\u003e40/45/50\u003c/b\u003e% missing healing progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/IconPerks_reactiveHealing.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Wiretap","description":"After repairing \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003e% of Generators, while next to a Generator, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to trap it for \u003cb\u003e100/110/120\u003c/b\u003es or until the Killer damages that Generator. All Survivors see that Generator\u0027s Aura for that time.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile the Killer is within \u003cb\u003e14\u003c/b\u003em of that Generator, all Survivors see the Killer\u0027s Aura.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/23/IconPerks_wiretap.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"adamfrancis","name":"Adam Francis","bio":"A resourceful teacher, able to adapt to new circumstances and develop strategies accordingly.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDiversion\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDeliverance\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eAutodidact\u003c/b\u003e, help him to distract The Killer, survive desperate situations, and become more skilled as the trial continues.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a5/S14_AdamFrancis_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Autodidact","description":"You start the trial with \u003cb\u003e0\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, up to \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003e, and your good basic healing Skill Checks give \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003e% less progress.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile healing another Survivor without a Med-Kit:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you hit a basic Skill Check, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e token.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you hit a basic Skill Check, for each Token, you gain \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou cannot get great basic Skill Checks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/96/IconPerks_autodidact.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5e/PerkAnimation_Autodidact_FifthToken.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Deliverance","description":"Once per trial, when you safely unhook another Survivor, you can unhook yourself. When you unhook yourself this way, you gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e160/140/120\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7e/IconPerks_deliverance.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/30/PerkAnimation_Deliverance_SelfUnhooking.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Diversion","description":"After hiding for \u003cb\u003e30/25/20\u003c/b\u003es within the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius, while crouched and idle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to throw a pebble \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003em away:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer is alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe pebble leaves Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a6/IconPerks_diversion.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4a/PerkAnimation_Diversion_KillerPOV.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"aestriyazar","name":"Aestri Yazar","bio":"Aestri, fellow bard Baermar, and their troupe never back down from any adventure.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTheir personal perks, \u003cb\u003eMirrored Illusion\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBardic Inspiration\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eStill Sight\u003c/b\u003e allow them to create illusions, help others repair generators quicker, and see nearby Killers, generators, and chests.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e0/S42_TheTroupe_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Bardic Inspiration","description":"While idle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to perform, empowering all Survivors within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em for up to \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es. While you are performing, other Survivors will see your Aura. Roll a d20:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e | You scream, but nothing happens.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003e2-10\u003c/b\u003e | Basic Skill Checks give +\u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e% progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003e11-19\u003c/b\u003e | Basic Skill Checks give +\u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e% progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e | Basic Skill Checks give +\u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e% progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you complete the performance, this effect ends after \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e110/100/90\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d8/IconPerks_bardicInspiration.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Mirrored Illusion","description":"After repairing \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% of Generators, while next to a Chest, Exit Gate Switch, Generator, or Totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to create a static illusion for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/97/IconPerks_mirroredIllusion.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Still Sight","description":"After being idle for \u003cb\u003e4/3/2\u003c/b\u003es, within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em, until you start moving:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Killer\u0027s Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Chests.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Generators.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b6/IconPerks_stillSight.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"alanwake","name":"Alan Wake","bio":"Alan Wake, bestselling author, knows what it means to push back the darkness.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis perks, \u003cb\u003eChampion of Light\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBoon: Illumination\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eDeadline\u003c/b\u003e, make Flashlights more powerful, reveal chests and generators, and create more frequent Skill Checks.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/43/S40_AlanWake_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Boon: Illumination","description":"While next to a totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to bless it, creating a unique Boon totem that combines all your Boons.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors within the Boon\u0027s range:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Auras of Chests.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Auras of Generators.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile you have a Boon Totem, you bless and cleanse \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8c/IconPerks_boonIllumination.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Champion of Light","description":"While you are using a Flashlight, you gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you blind the Killer, they gain \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bb/IconPerks_championOfLight.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Deadline","description":"While injured, basic Skill Checks:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAre \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003e% more likely to appear.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAppear in random places.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you miss a basic Skill Check, you lose \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% less progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1c/IconPerks_deadline.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"ashleyjwilliams","name":"Ashley J. Williams","bio":"An \"alone wolf,\" cocky and headstrong; a man built for survival.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eFlip-Flop\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBuckle Up\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eMettle of Man\u003c/b\u003e, give him additional resilience to pain and hardship, as well as the ability to help his friends out of sticky situations.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/43/New_Store_Ash.png","perks":[{"name":"Buckle Up","description":"While healing a downed Survivor, you both see the Killer\u0027s Aura.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you finish healing a downed Survivor or fully recover:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Survivor gains \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Survivor leaves no Scratch Marks for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/74/IconPerks_buckleUp.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Flip-Flop","description":"While downed, whenever the Killer picks you up, \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% of your recovery progress is added to your wiggle progress, up to \u003cb\u003e40/45/50\u003c/b\u003e%.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/31/IconPerks_flip-Flop.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b9/PerkAnimation_FlipFlop.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Mettle of Man","description":"After taking \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e protection hits, while injured and until you go down, the next time you would be downed by the Killer, take no damage instead.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you become healthy, while you are at least \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003em from the Killer, they see your Aura.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the trial starts, you are more likely to be the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/52/IconPerks_mettleOfMan.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c2/PerkAnimation_MettleOfMan_Hit.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"aurorastardotter","name":"Aurora Stardotter","bio":"Aurora Stardotter is viewed as a savior to her people and gains insight into the future by reading the stars.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eFruits of Your Labor\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSalvation\u0027s Cry\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBoon: Steadfast\u003c/b\u003e, allow for special advantages when completing Generators, strategic coordination during chases, and efficient Generator repairs.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"Boon: Steadfast","description":"While next to a Totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to bless it, creating a unique Boon Totem that combines all your Boons.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGenerators within the Boon\u0027s range:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eRegress \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors repair them \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors within the Boon\u0027s range see the Auras of affected Generators.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Fruits of Your Labor","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you finish repairing a Generator, for each Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e10/15/20\u003c/b\u003e% healing progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Salvation\u0027s Cry","description":"Whenever the Killer starts chasing you:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of other Survivors for \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors not being chased see your Aura for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors not being chased see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"cherylmason","name":"Cheryl Mason","bio":"Cheryl Mason is a young veteran of terror, emboldening both herself and her team.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eSoul Guard\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBlood Pact\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eRepressed Alliance\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to survive through immense hardship, stay in contact with team members, and plan objectives.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1d/S22_CherylMason_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Blood Pact","description":"While you are not the Obsession:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhile you or the Obsession are injured, you see each other\u0027s Auras.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you finish healing the Obsession, or they finish healing you, while within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em of each other, you both gain \u003cb\u003e5/6/7\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the trial starts, you are less likely to be the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c9/IconPerks_bloodPact.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6c/PerkAnimation_BloodPact_HealingObsession.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Repressed Alliance ","description":"After repairing Generators for \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es, while repairing a Generator alone, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to block that generator for \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/31/IconPerks_repressedAlliance.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f0/PerkAnimation_RepressedAlliance.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Soul Guard","description":"While hexed, you can fully recover.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you fully recover, you gain \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e4/6/8\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a5/IconPerks_soulGuard.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/97/PerkAnimation_SoulGuard.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"claudettemorel","name":"Claudette Morel","bio":"A studious botanist, able to boost her team\u0027s survivability as well as her own.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eEmpathy\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBotany Knowledge\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eSelf Care\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to spot injured Survivors and heal her team and herself more effectively.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c2/S03_ClaudetteMorel_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Botany Knowledge","description":"You heal \u003cb\u003e30/40/50\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1e/IconPerks_botanyKnowledge.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Empathy","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e64/96/128\u003c/b\u003em, you see the Auras of injured Survivors.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ae/IconPerks_empathy.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/50/PerkAnimation_Empathy.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Self-Care","description":"You can heal yourself, but \u003cb\u003e75/70/65\u003c/b\u003e% slower.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b2/IconPerks_self-Care.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/15/PerkAnimation_SelfCare.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"davidking","name":"David King","bio":"A rugged scrapper, rewarding high-risk play.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eWe\u0027re Gonna Live Forever\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDead Hard\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eNo Mither\u003c/b\u003e, reward an aggressive, confrontational playstyle but leave him vulnerable.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2a/S10_DavidKing_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dead Hard","description":"Whenever you are unhooked, while injured and running, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e0.5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/75/IconPerks_deadHard.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6c/PerkAnimation_DeadHard_Hit.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"No Mither","description":"When the trial starts, you become injured, then:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Grunts of Pain are \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% quieter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou recover \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou can fully recover.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f5/IconPerks_noMither.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9d/PerkAnimation_NoMither.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"We\u0027re Gonna Live Forever","description":"You heal downed Survivors \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you finish healing a downed Survivor, they gain \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b8/IconPerks_wereGonnaLiveForever.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/de/PerkAnimation_WGLF_FlashbangSave.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"detectivetapp","name":"Detective Tapp","bio":"An obsessed detective, able to locate and complete objectives faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eTenacity\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDetective\u0027s Hunch\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eStake Out\u003c/b\u003e, make him objective-focused and able to rapidly recover.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/71/New_Store_Tapp.png","perks":[{"name":"Detective\u0027s Hunch","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, for \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003es, within \u003cb\u003e32/48/64\u003c/b\u003em of you:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Chests.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Generators.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Totems.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7b/IconPerks_detectivesHunch.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ef/PerkAnimation_DetectivesHunch.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Stake Out","description":"After hiding for \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es within the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you hit a good basic Skill Check, spend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe good Skill Check becomes a great Skill Check.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cd/IconPerks_stakeOut.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4f/PerkAnimation_StakeOut_GettingTokens.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Tenacity","description":"While downed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e30/40/50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou can crawl and recover at the same time.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Grunts of Pain are \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% quieter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer cannot see your Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9d/IconPerks_tenacity.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/PerkAnimation_Tenacity.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"dustinhenderson","name":"Dustin Henderson","bio":"Dustin Henderson is a brilliant and somewhat nerdy high school student.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBada Bada Boom\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eChange of Plan\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTeamwork: Full Circuit\u003c/b\u003e allow him to slow down Killers, pivot his strategy mid-trial, and safely repair generators.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"Bada Bada Boom","description":"After repairing \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% of Generators, while next to a Window, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to trap it for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es. All Survivors see that Window\u0027s Aura for that time.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the Killer vaults that Window, the trap explodes and they gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Change of Plan","description":"When the trial starts, you earn \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e Tokens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile hiding in a Locker and holding a non-event Toolbox, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e and spend 1 Token to transform your Toolbox and add-ons into a Med-Kit of the same rarity with \u003cb\u003e80/90/100\u003c/b\u003e% Charges and random add-ons of the same rarity.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Teamwork: Full Circuit","description":"For each other Survivor repairing a Generator with you, good basic Skill Check zones are \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003e% bigger.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile repairing with at least 1 other Survivor, you repair \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"dwightfairfield","name":"Dwight Fairfield","bio":"A nervous leader, able to locate his allies and increase their effectiveness.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBond\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eProve Thyself\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eLeader\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to get in proximity of other Survivors and provide bonuses to their actions as well as his own.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3d/S01_DwightFairfield_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Bond","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e20/28/36\u003c/b\u003em, you see other Survivors\u0027 Auras.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a0/IconPerks_bond.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c6/PerkAnimation_Bond.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Leader","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003em of you, other Survivors:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eCleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eHeal \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOpen Exit Gates \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSabotage Hooks \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUnhook Survivors \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUnlock Chests \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter they leave your range, this ends after \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3d/IconPerks_leader.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/18/PerkAnimation_Leader_Cleansing.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Prove Thyself","description":"For each other Survivor within \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003em of you, all Survivors repair \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0f/IconPerks_proveThyself.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"eleven","name":"Eleven","bio":"Eleven is a former test subject with extrasensory abilities.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eExtrasensory Perception\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eWe See You\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTeamwork: Soft-Spoken\u003c/b\u003e allow her to scout the area, reveal the Killer\u0027s aura, and reduce the noise of generators.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"Extrasensory Perception","description":"After crouching for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see Auras in an expanding radius up to \u003cb\u003e44\u003c/b\u003em.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eElusive\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eOblivious\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you stop crouching, or after \u003cb\u003e11\u003c/b\u003es, cooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Teamwork: Soft-Spoken","description":"For each other Survivor repairing a Generator with you, the range of Generator repair noises is \u003cb\u003e15/20/25\u003c/b\u003e% smaller.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile repairing with at least 1 other Survivor, you repair \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"We See You","description":"Whenever the Killer sees your Aura, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you have \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, spend them all. Then, all Survivors see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e10/12.5/15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"ellenripley","name":"Ellen Ripley","bio":"Ellen Ripley, Warrant Officer of the Nostromo, is capable and pragmatic. Her personal perks, \u003cb\u003eLucky Star\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eChemical Trap\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eLight-footed\u003c/b\u003e let her hide her pools of blood and grunts of pain, slow Killers with trapped pallets, and run silently.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/15/S39_EllenRipley_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Chemical Trap","description":"After repairing \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% of Generators, while next to a Dropped Pallet, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to trap it for \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es. All Survivors see that Pallet\u0027s Aura for that time.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the Killer breaks that Pallet, the trap explodes and they gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHindered\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9a/IconPerks_chemicalTrap.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Light-footed","description":"While healthy and running, your footsteps are silent to the Killer.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you do a fast-action, cooldown: \u003cb\u003e14/12/10\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e5/IconPerks_light-Footed.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Lucky Star","description":"While hiding in a Locker, you make no Grunts of Pain.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you exit a Locker, for \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Aura of the closest Generator.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of other Survivors.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou make no Grunts of Pain.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e35/30/25\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/08/IconPerks_luckyStar.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"lodierakoto","name":"Élodie Rakoto","bio":"An occult investigator, able to use cunning tricks and stubborn resolve to keep herself alive.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eAppraisal\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDeception\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003ePower Struggle\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to interact with objects in new ways, all while having a backup plan to escape Killers.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/de/S24_ElodieRakoto_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Appraisal","description":"When the trial starts, you earn \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e Tokens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSpend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token to rummage an empty Chest, up to \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e times per Chest.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou rummage Chests \u003cb\u003e40/60/80\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c1/IconPerks_appraisal.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d7/PerkAnimation_Appraisal.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Deception","description":"Whenever you attempt to fast-enter a Locker:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou do not enter the Locker.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer is alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Scratch Marks for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e25/20/15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/eb/IconPerks_deception.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/08/PerkAnimation_Deception.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Power Struggle","description":"While carried by the Killer, while you have at least \u003cb\u003e25/20/15\u003c/b\u003e% wiggle and next to an Upright Pallet, you can drop it to stun the Killer.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile downed, you see the Auras of Upright Pallets.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4b/IconPerks_powerStruggle.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d0/PerkAnimation_PowerStruggle.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"felixrichter","name":"Felix Richter","bio":"A visionary architect, able to use his relentless determination to form a plan and help other Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eVisionary\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDesperate Measures\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBuilt to Last\u003c/b\u003e, help him reveal generators, rescue Survivors, and get the most from his tools.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9e/S23_FelixRichter_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Built to Last","description":"While holding a depleted item, after hiding in a Locker for \u003cb\u003e14/12/10\u003c/b\u003es, it is recharged to \u003cb\u003e99\u003c/b\u003e%.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEach time you recharge an item this way, it recharges \u003cb\u003e33\u003c/b\u003e% fewer Charges.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/IconPerks_builtToLast.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2b/PerkAnimation_BuiltToLast_Refill1.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Desperate Measures","description":"For each injured, downed, or hooked Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou heal \u003cb\u003e16/18/20\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unhook \u003cb\u003e16/18/20\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/84/IconPerks_desperateMeasures.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Visionary","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e32\u003c/b\u003em of you, you see the Auras of Generators.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Generator is completed, cooldown: \u003cb\u003e20/18/16\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7c/IconPerks_visionary.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7f/PerkAnimation_Visionary.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"fengmin","name":"Feng Min","bio":"An objective-focused competitor who can quickly adapt her strategy to meet a vast range of challenging situations.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eTechnician\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eLithe\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eAlert\u003c/b\u003e, help her with repairing generators and locating the Killer.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a3/S09_FengMin_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Alert","description":"Whenever the Killer breaks a Pallet or Breakable Wall, or damages a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou hear a sound cue.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/71/IconPerks_alert.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/af/PerkAnimation_Alert_BreakableWall.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Lithe","description":"Whenever you medium or fast-vault:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cc/IconPerks_lithe.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f7/PerkAnimation_Lithe.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Technician","description":"While repairing a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe range of Generator repair noises is \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em shorter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you miss a basic Skill Check, the Generator does not explode, but loses \u003cb\u003e4/3/2\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/62/IconPerks_technician.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6a/PerkAnimation_Technician.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"gabrielsoma","name":"Gabriel Soma","bio":"A resourceful engineer, ready to make the most out of any situation.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eTroubleshooter\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eMade For This\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eScavenger\u003c/b\u003e, help him see things during a chase, gain Endurance after healing Survivors, and recharge his toolbox.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/64/S37_GabrielSoma_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Made for This","description":"While injured, whenever you finish healing another Survivor, you gain \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile you are running and have \u003cb\u003eDeep Wound\u003c/b\u003e, you gain \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c0/IconPerks_madeForThis.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Scavenger","description":"While repairing and while your Toolbox is empty, whenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you have \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, spend them all:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Toolbox is recharged instantly.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou repair \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% slower for \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou can rummage Chests \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e time. The first time you rummage a Chest, it will contain an uncommon Toolbox.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c6/IconPerks_scavenger.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Troubleshooter","description":"While chased by the Killer:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Aura of the Generator with the most progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you drop a Pallet, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the Killer stops chasing you, this ends after \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0d/IconPerks_troubleshooter.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"haddiekaur","name":"Haddie Kaur","bio":"Haddie is a brave and determined podcaster with the ability to see and feel places of great suffering she calls Overlaps.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eInner Focus\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eResidual Manifest\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eOverzealous\u003c/b\u003e allow her to track Survivors and Killers after an attack, use Flashlights more effectively, and repair generators more efficiently.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e7/S31_HaddieKaur_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Inner Focus","description":"Whenever the Killer damages another Survivor, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see other Survivors\u0027 Scratch Marks.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7e/IconPerks_innerFocus.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Overzealous","description":"Whenever you bless or cleanse a Totem, until you take damage, you repair \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster. If that Totem was a Hex Totem, the effect is doubled.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/99/IconPerks_overzealous.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Residual Manifest","description":"Whenever you blind the Killer, they gain \u003cb\u003eBlindness\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou can rummage Chests \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e time. The first time you rummage a Chest, it will contain an uncommon Flashlight.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d0/IconPerks_residualManifest.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"jakepark","name":"Jake Park","bio":"A solitary survivalist, able to hold his own in most situations.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eIron Will\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCalm Spirit\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eSaboteur\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to more effectively move about the environment and survive while injured.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/18/S04_JakePark_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Calm Spirit","description":"You do not scare Crows or scream.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou bless and cleanse Totems, and unlock Chests silently, but \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003e% slower.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6c/IconPerks_calmSpirit.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7e/PerkAnimation_CalmSpirit_Crows.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Iron Will","description":"While injured and not \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e, your Grunts of Pain are \u003cb\u003e80/90/100\u003c/b\u003e% quieter.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/58/IconPerks_ironWill.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2a/PerkAnimation_IronWill.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Saboteur","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e56\u003c/b\u003em of where another Survivor was picked-up by the Killer and is being carried, you see the Auras of Hooks and Scourge Hooks.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou can sabotage Hooks. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e70/65/60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0e/IconPerks_saboteur.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e1/PerkAnimation_Saboteur.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"janeromero","name":"Jane Romero","bio":"An influential celebrity, going against the grain to tackle challenges head on.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eSolidarity\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003ePoised\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eHead On\u003c/b\u003e, give her a flexible skillset that allow her to help others, as well as herself, to escape dangerous situations.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/80/S16_JaneRomero_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Head On","description":"After hiding in a Locker for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es, fast-exit to stun the Killer for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es if they are within \u003cb\u003e2.5\u003c/b\u003em, then gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cb/IconPerks_headOn.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/22/PerkAnimation_HeadOn_KillerPOV.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Poised","description":"The first time you start repairing each Generator, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Generator is completed, you leave no Scratch Marks for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/52/IconPerks_poised.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f0/PerkAnimation_Poised.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Solidarity","description":"While injured and healing another Survivor without a Med-Kit, you also gain healing progress at \u003cb\u003e50/60/70\u003c/b\u003e% speed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9e/IconPerks_solidarity.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/19/PerkAnimation_Solidarity.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"jeffjohansen","name":"Jeff Johansen","bio":"A quiet artist, standing steadfast against impossible odds.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBreakdown\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eAftercare\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eDistortion\u003c/b\u003e, give him observational advantages and help to hide his presence from The Killer.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/81/S15_JeffJohansen_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Aftercare","description":"You and up to \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003e Survivors see each other\u0027s Auras whenever:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unhook them, or they unhook you.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou finish healing them, or they finish healing you.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis effect lasts until you are hooked.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0d/IconPerks_aftercare.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8d/PerkAnimation_Aftercare.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Breakdown","description":"Whenever you are unhooked:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Hook breaks, then is repaired after \u003cb\u003e180\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6c/IconPerks_breakdown.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b3/PerkAnimation_Breakdown.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Distortion","description":"When the trial starts, and after being chased for \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile not downed, whenever the Killer attempts to see your Aura, spend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token. Then, for the next \u003cb\u003e8/10/12\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer cannot see your Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/41/IconPerks_distortion.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b5/PerkAnimation_Distortion.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"jillvalentine","name":"Jill Valentine","bio":"Jill Valentine is a founding member of S.T.A.R.S. who has triumphed over countless bio-organic weapons.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eCounterforce\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eResurgence\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBlast Mine\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to indirectly fight back, while offering strong support to her teammates.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/db/S26_JillValentine_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Blast Mine","description":"After repairing \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003e% of Generators, while next to a Generator, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to trap it for \u003cb\u003e100/110/120\u003c/b\u003es. All Survivors see that Generator\u0027s Aura for that time.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the Killer damages that Generator, the trap explodes, then:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey are stunned for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eEveryone nearby looking at the detonation is blinded.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1c/IconPerks_blastMine.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/68/PerkAnimation_BlastMine_Activated.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Counterforce","description":"When the trial starts, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you cleanse a Totem, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, then, you see the Aura of the farthest Totem for \u003cb\u003e10/12/14\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, you cleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d1/IconPerks_counterforce.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fc/PerkAnimation_Counterforce_1.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Resurgence","description":"Whenever you are unhooked, you gain \u003cb\u003e50/60/70\u003c/b\u003e% healing progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f3/IconPerks_resurgence.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/85/PerkAnimation_Resurgence.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"jonahvasquez","name":"Jonah Vasquez","bio":"Jonah is a mathematical mastermind, able to use logic to help his team.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eOvercome\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCorrective Action\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBoon: Exponential\u003c/b\u003e allow him to quickly flee, correct failed skill checks, and treat dying Survivors.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/37/S29_JonahVasquez_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Boon: Exponential","description":"While next to a Totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to bless it, creating a unique Boon Totem that combines all your Boons.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDowned Survivors within the Boon\u0027s range:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eRecover \u003cb\u003e90/95/100\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCan fully recover.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/76/IconPerks_boonExponential.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/PerkAnimation_BoonExponential_Recovering.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Corrective Action","description":"When the trial starts, you earn \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, up to \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever another Survivor misses a basic Skill Check, spend \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe missed Skill Check becomes a good Skill Check.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see that Survivor\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4f/IconPerks_correctiveAction.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Overcome","description":"Whenever you take damage:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou retain your speed boost for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es longer.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/82/IconPerks_overcome.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bd/PerkAnimation_Overcome.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"katedenson","name":"Kate Denson","bio":"A hopeful songbird, able to make the most of her surroundings.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDance With Me\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eWindows of Opportunity\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eBoil Over\u003c/b\u003e, grant her the foresight and feistiness to escape even the most dire situations.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9c/S13_KateDenson_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Boil Over","description":"While carried by the Killer:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever the Killer falls from at least \u003cb\u003e1.25\u003c/b\u003em, you gain \u003cb\u003e33\u003c/b\u003e% of your current wiggle progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour wiggle is \u003cb\u003e60/70/80\u003c/b\u003e% stronger.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em, the Killer cannot see Hook Auras.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f5/IconPerks_boilOver.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b5/PerkAnimation_BoilOver.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Dance With Me","description":"Whenever you fast-exit a Locker, medium-vault, or fast-vault, you leave no Scratch Marks for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e25/20/15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/17/IconPerks_danceWithMe.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/06/PerkAnimation_DanceWithMe_Locker.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Windows of Opportunity","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e24/28/32\u003c/b\u003em of you:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Pallets.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Breakable Walls.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Windows.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/17/IconPerks_windowsOfOpportunity.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6e/PerkAnimation_WindowsOfOpportunity.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"kwontaeyoung","name":"Kwon Tae-young","bio":"Kwon Tae-young is a hard-working perfectionist who does not rest until he gets results.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eFlow State\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eA Place For Us\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eFive Moves Ahead\u003c/b\u003e allow him to ramp up his efficiency as generators are completed; heal others, especially the Obsession, covertly; and make more informed decisions when within the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"A Place For Us","description":"While healing another Survivor, you both gain \u003cb\u003eElusive\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you finish healing the Obsession, you both gain \u003cb\u003eElusive\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the trial starts, you are less likely to be the Obsession.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Five Moves Ahead","description":"While you are in the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius or chased by the Killer:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of the \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e closest Pallets and Windows.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAfter you drop a Pallet, you start moving \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% earlier.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you drop a Pallet, cooldown: \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Flow State","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou bless and cleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou heal \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unhook Survivors \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"laracroft","name":"Lara Croft","bio":"Lara Croft\u0027s instincts have been honed by her many dangerous expeditions.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eFinesse\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSpecialist\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHardened\u003c/b\u003e allow her to reveal the killer instead of screaming, repair generators more efficiently, and fast vault faster.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/63/S43_LaraCroft_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Finesse","description":"While healthy, you fast-vault \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you fast-vault, cooldown: \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fc/IconPerks_finesse.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/48/PerkAnimation_Finesse.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hardened","description":"When you have blessed or cleansed a Totem and unlocked a Chest, whenever you would scream, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es instead.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fe/IconPerks_hardened.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Specialist","description":"Whenever you rummage or unlock a Chest, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile repairing a Generator, whenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, spend all Tokens. For each Token spent, the Generator gains \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e% permanent progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ae/IconPerks_specialist.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"lauriestrode","name":"Laurie Strode","bio":"A determined Survivor, prepared to weather any challenge.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eSole Survivor\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eObject of Obsession\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eDecisive Strike\u003c/b\u003e, grant her powerful survival abilities at the cost of leaving her exposed.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/04/S06_LaurieStrode_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Decisive Strike","description":"Until all Generators are completed, whenever you are unhooked, for the next \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es: when the Killer picks you up, once per trial, hit a Special Skill check:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eStun the Killer for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBecome the Obsession.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis is disabled by conspicuous actions. At the start of the trial, you are more likely to be the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ee/IconPerks_decisiveStrike.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/81/PerkAnimation_DecisiveStrike_Deactivating.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Object of Obsession","description":"While you are the Obsession, every \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es, the Killer sees your Aura for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile the Killer sees your Aura:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see their Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou cleanse totems \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou heal \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou repair \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the trial starts, you are more likely to be the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2b/IconPerks_objectOfObsession.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/56/PerkAnimation_ObjectOfObsession.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Sole Survivor","description":"Whenever a Survivor dies, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, within \u003cb\u003e20/22/24\u003c/b\u003em, the Killer cannot see your Aura.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all other Survivors are dead:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou repair \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou open Exit Gates and the Hatch \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the trial starts, you are more likely to be the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8e/IconPerks_soleSurvivor.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"leeyunjin","name":"Lee Yun-jin","bio":"A self-interested music producer, able to advance her goals during turbulent times.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eFast Track\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSmash Hit\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eSelf-Preservation\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to improve her abilities when others are harmed, and quickly escape from a chase.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f7/S25_Yun-JinLee_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Fast Track","description":"Whenever you unhook another Survivor, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile repairing, whenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, spend all Tokens. For each Token spent, the Generator gains \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% permanent progress.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/75/IconPerks_fastTrack.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8f/PerkAnimation_FastTrack.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Self-Preservation","description":"Whenever another Survivor is hooked, you gain \u003cb\u003eElusive\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/43/IconPerks_self-Preservation.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/98/PerkAnimation_SelfPreservation.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Smash Hit","description":"Whenever you Pallet-stun the Killer:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30/25/20\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e0/IconPerks_smashHit.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/43/PerkAnimation_SmashHit.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"leonskennedy","name":"Leon S. Kennedy","bio":"Leon S. Kennedy is a rookie police officer who went beyond the call of duty during the outbreak in Raccoon City.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBite the Bullet\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eFlashbang\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eRookie Spirit\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to ignore pain, disorient the Killer, and track objectives being lost.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b3/New_Store_Leon.png","perks":[{"name":"Bite the Bullet","description":"While healing, you and the healed Survivor make no noises or Grunts of Pain. Whenever you miss a basic Skill Check:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou lose only \u003cb\u003e3/2/1\u003c/b\u003e% progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer is not alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a5/IconPerks_biteTheBullet.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6d/PerkAnimation_BiteTheBullet.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Flashbang","description":"After repairing \u003cb\u003e50/45/40\u003c/b\u003e% of Generators, while hiding in a Locker, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to craft a Flashbang.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you use the Flashbang:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eEveryone nearby looking at the detonation is blinded.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer is alerted.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/db/IconPerks_flashbang.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/19/PerkAnimation_Flashbang.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Rookie Spirit","description":"After you hit \u003cb\u003e5/4/3\u003c/b\u003e basic repair Skill Checks, while a Generator is regressing, you see its Aura.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2f/IconPerks_rookieSpirit.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/77/PerkAnimation_RookieSpirit.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"megthomas","name":"Meg Thomas","bio":"An energetic athlete, able to outrun most Killers.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eQuick \u0026 Quiet\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eSprint Burst\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eAdrenaline\u003c/b\u003e, give her advantage to escape chases and put distance between herself and the Killer.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/35/S02_MegThomas_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Adrenaline","description":"When all Generators are completed, if you are downed or injured, heal instantly. Then, ignoring \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f7/IconPerks_adrenaline.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/21/PerkAnimation_Adrenaline_WhileDyingState.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Quick \u0026 Quiet","description":"You hide in Lockers and vault silently. The Killer is not alerted. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e25/20/15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/14/IconPerks_quickAndQuiet.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/29/PerkAnimation_Quick%26Quiet_Vaulting.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Sprint Burst","description":"Whenever you start running:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e4/IconPerks_sprintBurst.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1e/PerkAnimation_SprintBurst.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"michonnegrimes","name":"Michonne Grimes","bio":"Michonne Grimes is a relentless protector living in a community of post-apocalyptic survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eConviction\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eLast Stand\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTeamwork: Throw Down\u003c/b\u003e allow her to make one last push after being downed, stun the Killer with a fast vault, and empower other Survivors after a tense chase.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/aa/S47_MichonneGrimes_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Conviction","description":"After you finish healing \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e other Survivor, while downed with at least \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% recovery, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to recover instantly.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e, then, after \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es, you are downed instantly.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Last Stand","description":"After hiding for \u003cb\u003e120/105/90\u003c/b\u003es within the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius, when you fast-vault, once per trial, stun the Killer for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es if they are within \u003cb\u003e2.5\u003c/b\u003em.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Teamwork: Throw Down","description":"Whenever you blind or Pallet-stun the Killer, for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es, other injured Survivors within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Killer\u0027s Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"mikaelareid","name":"Mikaela Reid","bio":"Mikaela is a young mystic, able to alter the trial with supernatural abilities.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eClairvoyance\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBoon: Circle of Healing\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBoon: Shadow Step\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to oversee the area while creating places of refuge.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3f/S28_MikaelaReid_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Boon: Circle of Healing","description":"While next to a Totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to bless it, creating a unique Boon Totem that combines all your Boons.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors within the Boon\u0027s range:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhile healing without a Med-Kit, they heal others \u003cb\u003e50/75/100\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhile injured, other Survivors see their Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/54/IconPerks_boonCircleOfHealing.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9f/PerkAnimation_BoonCoH_AltruisticHealing.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Boon: Shadow Step","description":"While next to a Totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to bless it, creating a unique Boon Totem that combines all your Boons. Survivors within the Boon\u0027s range:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eLeave no Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eTheir Auras cannot be seen by the Killer.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen leaving the range, this ends after \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c7/IconPerks_boonShadowStep.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/74/PerkAnimation_BoonShadowStep_ScratchMarks.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Clairvoyance","description":"Whenever you bless or cleanse a Totem, while not holding an item, use \u003cb\u003eUse Item\u003c/b\u003e to, for up to \u003cb\u003e10/11/12\u003c/b\u003es and within \u003cb\u003e64\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Auras of Chests.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Auras of Exit Gate Switches.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Auras of Generators.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Aura of the Hatch.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSee the Auras of Hooks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/91/IconPerks_clairvoyance.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/24/PerkAnimation_Clairvoyance.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"nancywheeler","name":"Nancy Wheeler","bio":"An aspiring journalist, able to make acute observations and gain insights that others may miss.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer perks, \u003cb\u003eBetter Together\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eFixated\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eInner Strength\u003c/b\u003e, give her the information and courage she needs to tackle unexpected challenges.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/70/S18_NancyWheeler_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Better Together","description":"While you are repairing a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eOther Survivors see that Generator\u0027s Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever the Killer downs a Survivor, you see the Auras of all Survivors for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/02/IconPerks_betterTogether.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Fixated","description":"While walking, you gain \u003cb\u003e10/15/20\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see your own Scratch Marks.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7c/IconPerks_fixated.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/27/PerkAnimation_Fixated_MovementSpeed.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Inner Strength","description":"Whenever you cleanse a Totem, while injured and not \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e, after hiding in a Locker for \u003cb\u003e10/9/8\u003c/b\u003es, you become healthy instantly.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/47/IconPerks_innerStrength.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"neakarlsson","name":"Nea Karlsson","bio":"An urban artist, able to easily escape and hide.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBalanced Landing\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eUrban Evasion\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eStreetwise\u003c/b\u003e, make her well suited to completing objectives and rapid evasion.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e6/S05_NeaKarlsson_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Balanced Landing","description":"Whenever you fall from at least \u003cb\u003e1.25\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour stagger is \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% shorter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Grunts from falling are \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% quieter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5e/IconPerks_balancedLanding.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/86/PerkAnimation_BalancedLanding.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Streetwise","description":"The first time you deplete an item\u0027s Charges, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you loot an item from a Chest, it has \u003cb\u003e60/70/80\u003c/b\u003e% more Charges.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/ff/IconPerks_streetwise.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/11/PerkAnimation_Streetwise.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Urban Evasion","description":"While crouched, you gain \u003cb\u003e90/95/100\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c7/IconPerks_urbanEvasion.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/18/PerkAnimation_UrbanEvasion.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"nicolascage","name":"Nicolas Cage","bio":"Nicolas Cage is a superstar, trapped in the role of a lifetime.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDramaturgy\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eScene Partner\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003ePlot Twist\u003c/b\u003e, help him make a quick escape, see the Killer’s aura, and pretend to be dying.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b7/S38_NicolasCage_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Dramaturgy","description":"While healthy and running, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThen, one happens at random:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain a random rare item with random add-ons.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou scream, but nothing happens.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe same effect cannot happen twice in a row.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/85/IconPerks_dramaturgy.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Plot Twist","description":"While injured, crouched and idle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to be downed silently.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile downed this way, once per trial:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou make no Grunts of Pain.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou recover \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou can fully recover.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you recover this way:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou are healed instantly.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all Generators are completed, you can use this ability once again.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ac/IconPerks_plotTwist.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Scene Partner","description":"While you are within the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius, whenever you look at them:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eScream, then see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThere is a \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% chance you will scream again. If you do, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es more.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b4/IconPerks_scenePartner.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"orelarose","name":"Orela Rose","bio":"Orela Rose is a paramedic with a love for horror and a calming demeanor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eDo No Harm\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eDuty of Care\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eRapid Response\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to heal Survivors faster, give Haste to other Survivors, and see the Killer’s aura upon gaining Exhausted.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/38/S46_OrelaRose_Portrait.webp/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Do No Harm","description":"While healing another Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eFor each Hook State they have, you heal \u003cb\u003e30/40/50\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, you gain \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Duty of Care","description":"While healthy, whenever you take a protection hit, other Survivors within \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003em gain \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Rapid Response","description":"Whenever you fast-exit a Locker, you gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30/25/20\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you gain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"quentinsmith","name":"Quentin Smith","bio":"A resolute dreamwalker, increasing the survivability and recovery of his team.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eWake Up!\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003ePharmacy\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eVigil\u003c/b\u003e, help Survivors locate exit gates and recover more easily.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/40/S11_QuentinSmith_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Pharmacy","description":"Whenever you unlock a Chest, it will contain a rare Med-Kit.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou unlock Chests \u003cb\u003e75/100/125\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe range at which the Killer hears you unlocking Chests is \u003cb\u003e12\u003c/b\u003em shorter.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f1/IconPerks_pharmacy.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/47/PerkAnimation_Pharmacy.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Vigil","description":"All Survivors within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em of you lose \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis effect ends \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es after they leave your range.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/46/IconPerks_vigil.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/df/PerkAnimation_Vigil.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Wake Up!","description":"When all Generators are completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of Exit Gate Switches.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhile opening an Exit Gate, other Survivors see your Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eFor each Survivor alive, you open Exit Gates \u003cb\u003e8/10/12.5\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fd/IconPerks_wakeUp.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/63/PerkAnimation_WakeUp%21.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"rebeccachambers","name":"Rebecca Chambers","bio":"Rebecca Chambers is a gifted medic and squad member whose presence soothes those around her.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBetter Than New\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eReassurance\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eHyperfocus\u003c/b\u003e allow her to give her teammates speed boosts, give temporary relief to struggling allies, and complete skill checks at increased speed.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fd/S33_RebeccaChambers_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Better Than New","description":"Whenever you finish healing another Survivor, until they take damage:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey bless and cleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey heal \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey unlock Chests \u003cb\u003e12/14/16\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b1/IconPerks_betterThanNew.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hyperfocus","description":"Whenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, basic Skill Checks:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAppear \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e% more often.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eSpin \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you hit a great, give \u003cb\u003e10/20/30\u003c/b\u003e% more progress.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you miss a basic Skill Check, hit a good Skill Check, or stop healing or repairing, lose all Tokens.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5d/IconPerks_hyperfocus.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Reassurance","description":"Once per Hook State, while within \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003em of a hooked Survivor, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to stop the sacrifice progress for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5b/IconPerks_reassurance.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"renatolyra","name":"Renato Lyra","bio":"Renato always keeps his eye on the prize, and he expects the same from his teammates.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eBackground Player\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBlood Rush\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTeamwork: Collective Stealth\u003c/b\u003e allow him to move faster when near a chase, recover from Exhausted instantly, and hide your and an allies\u0027 scratch marks after that ally heals you.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/69/S36_RenatoLyra_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Background Player","description":"Whenever the Killer picks-up another Survivor, for the next \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es, when you start running:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eGain \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e30/25/20\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e8/IconPerks_backgroundPlayer.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Blood Rush","description":"Until all Generators are completed, whenever you are unhooked, for the next \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es, while \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to lose \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e instantly.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis is disabled by conspicuous actions.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2c/IconPerks_bloodRush.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Teamwork: Collective Stealth","description":"Whenever another Survivor finishes healing you, while within \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003em of each other, you both leave no Scratch Marks. When either of you leaves the range, this ends after \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a0/IconPerks_teamworkCollectiveStealth.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"rickgrimes","name":"Rick Grimes","bio":"Rick Grimes is the leader of a group of post-apocalyptic survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eApocalyptic Ingenuity\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCome and Get Me!\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTeamwork: Toughen Up\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to remake broken pallets, help vulnerable teammates, and be discreet when injured.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4f/S46_RickGrimes_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Apocalyptic Ingenuity","description":"After you rummage or unlock \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Chest, while next to a Broken Pallet, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es to create a Fragile Pallet.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e24/28/32\u003c/b\u003em, you see the Auras of Broken Pallets.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Come and Get Me!","description":"Whenever you unhook a Survivor, while crouched and idle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to have injured and downed Survivors within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eMake no Grunts of Pain for \u003cb\u003e10/12.5/15\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLeave no Pools of Blood for \u003cb\u003e10/12.5/15\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eLeave no Scratch Marks for \u003cb\u003e10/12.5/15\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou scream, then the Killer sees your Aura for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Teamwork: Toughen Up","description":"While injured, whenever another Survivor within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em of you blinds or Pallet-stuns the Killer, for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou make no Grunts of Pain.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"sableward","name":"Sable Ward","bio":"Sable is not afraid to embrace the darkness, or the power that lies within it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eInvocation: Weaving Spiders\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eStrength in Shadows\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eWicked\u003c/b\u003e allow her to quicken repair progress, heal herself without a Med-kit, and escape the basement hooks.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9c/S41_SableWard_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Invocation: Weaving Spiders","description":"While in the Basement next to the circle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to invoke. While invoking, other Survivors see your Aura and can join your Invocation.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the Invocation is completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAll Generators gain \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e permanent charges.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou become injured.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEach Invocation can only be completed once per trial.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/07/IconPerks_invocationWeavingSpiders.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Strength in Shadows","description":"While in the Basement:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou can heal yourself, but \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you finish healing, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e2/IconPerks_strengthInShadows.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Wicked","description":"While in the Basement, you can unhook yourself.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you are unhooked, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e16/18/20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8f/IconPerks_wicked.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"shanewiigwaas","name":"Shane Wiigwaas","bio":"Shane Wiigwaas follows his own road, hoping to atone for his past mistakes.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eWide Open Throttle\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eLend a Hand\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eCross-Examination\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to reset dropped pallets, give permanent healing charges, and see Light Marks left behind by the Killer.","portrait":null,"perks":[{"name":"Cross-Examination","description":"While in the Killer\u0027s Terror Radius and not being chased by the Killer, they leave Light Marks that last for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es that you can see. While on the Killer\u0027s Light Marks, you gain \u003cb\u003eElusive\u003c/b\u003e. This ends after \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Lend a Hand","description":"Whenever you bless or cleanse \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Totem, while healing another Survivor and only once per Survivor, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to give them \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e permanent healing charges.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Wide Open Throttle","description":"Whenever you fast-vault a Pallet:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e10/12.5/15\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Pallet is reset, blocked for \u003cb\u003e60\u003c/b\u003es, and all Survivors see its Aura for that time.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e60\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"steveharrington","name":"Steve Harrington","bio":"A former jock, able to protect and support his fellow Survivors while providing his own brand of humor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis perks, \u003cb\u003eBabysitter\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eCamaraderie\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eSecond Wind\u003c/b\u003e, enable him to distract Killers, tolerate pain, and get back into the fight.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e8/S19_SteveHarrington_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Babysitter","description":"Whenever you unhook a Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey leave no Pools of Blood for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey leave no Scratch Marks for \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e8\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/db/IconPerks_babysitter.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ad/PerkAnimation_Guardian.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Camaraderie","description":"While you are struggling on Hook, when another Survivor gets within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em, the timer is paused for \u003cb\u003e26/30/34\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1d/IconPerks_camaraderie.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/30/PerkAnimation_Kinship.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Second Wind","description":"After you heal \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Survivor, while not \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e, when you are unhooked, you gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter \u003cb\u003e28/24/20\u003c/b\u003es, if you are not downed, you are instantly healed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/97/IconPerks_secondWind.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3b/PerkAnimation_Renewal.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"tauriecain","name":"Taurie Cain","bio":"Taurie Cain was raised as a Disciple of the Black Talon, condemned to be a sacrifice.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eInvocation: Treacherous Crows\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eClean Break\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eShoulder the Burden\u003c/b\u003e, allow her to reveal the Killer\u0027s aura, heal after being Broken, and take on another Survivor’s hook state.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/72/S45_TaurieCain_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Clean Break","description":"Whenever you finish healing another Survivor, while being healed by another Survivor, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter \u003cb\u003e75/60/45\u003c/b\u003es, if you are not downed, you are instantly healed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b3/IconPerks_cleanBreak.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Invocation: Treacherous Crows","description":"While in the Basement next to the circle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to invoke. While invoking, other Survivors see your Aura and can join your Invocation.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the Invocation is completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever the Killer scares a Crow while a Survivor is in their Terror Radius, all Survivors see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e1/1.5/2\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou become injured.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEach Invocation can only be completed once per trial.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a8/IconPerks_invocationTreacherousCrows.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Shoulder the Burden","description":"Once per trial, while you do not have \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003e Hook States and are next to a hooked Survivor, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to unhook them:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey lose 1 Hook State.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain 1 Hook State.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou scream.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e60/50/40\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3a/IconPerks_shoulderTheBurden.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"thalitalyra","name":"Thalita Lyra","bio":"Thalita has mastered the art of competitive flair, fighting kites with skill and flourish.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eCut Loose\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eFriendly Competition\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eTeamwork: Power of Two\u003c/b\u003e allow her to perform a series of fast vaults, inspire faster generator repair from teammates, and help allies move faster after they are healed by you.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/96/S35_ThalitaLyra_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Cut Loose","description":"While chased by the Killer, whenever you medium or fast-vault:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eFor up to \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es, your medium and fast vaults are silent.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eDuring that time, whenever you medium or fast-vault, the timer is reset.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e45\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/02/IconPerks_cutLoose.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Friendly Competition","description":"Whenever you finish repairing a Generator with at least 1 other Survivor, Survivors who finished repairing it repair \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% faster for \u003cb\u003e100/110/120\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4c/IconPerks_friendlyCompetition.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Teamwork: Power of Two","description":"Whenever you finish healing another Survivor, while you stay within \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003em of each other, you both gain \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e. When either of you leaves the range, this ends after \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2b/IconPerks_teamworkPowerOfTwo.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"trevorbelmont","name":"Trevor Belmont","bio":"Trevor Belmont, vampire hunter, knows his destiny is to vanquish evil. His personal perks, \u003cb\u003eEyes of Belmont\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eExultation\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eMoment of Glory\u003c/b\u003e, allow him to see the Killer\u0027s aura, increase an item\u0027s rarity, and heal one health state.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f8/S44_TrevorBelmont_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Exultation","description":"Whenever you Pallet-stun the Killer:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour item rarity is upgraded to the next tier, if possible.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf the item was upgraded, it recharges \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% Charges.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCooldown: \u003cb\u003e30/25/20\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/22/IconPerks_Exultation.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Eyes of Belmont","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e1/2/3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for a duration, it is \u003cb\u003e2\u003c/b\u003es longer.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/25/IconPerks_EyesOfBelmont.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Moment of Glory","description":"After you rummage or unlock \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Chest, while not \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e, when you become injured, gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAfter \u003cb\u003e80/70/60\u003c/b\u003es, if you are not downed, you are instantly healed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/98/IconPerks_MomentOfGlory.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"veeboonyasak","name":"Vee Boonyasak","bio":"Vee Boonyasak is an energetic drummer whose adventurous nature led to a doomed concert.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eRoad Life\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eONE-TWO-THREE-FOUR!\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eGhost Notes\u003c/b\u003e allow her to leverage repair work into faster healing, strengthen allies\u0027 ability to repair and heal, and recover from Exhausted faster.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/ce/S48_VeeBoonyasak_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Ghost Notes","description":"While you have \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e, your Scratch Marks disappear \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou lose \u003cb\u003eExhausted\u003c/b\u003e \u003cb\u003e5/7.5/10\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"ONE-TWO-THREE-FOUR!","description":"While idle, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to perform, empowering all Survivors within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em for up to \u003cb\u003e15\u003c/b\u003es. While you are performing, other Survivors will see your Aura. You get special Skill Checks during that time: while healing or repairing, basic Skill Checks are \u003cb\u003e20\u003c/b\u003e% more likely to appear.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIf you complete the performance, the effect ends after \u003cb\u003e90\u003c/b\u003es. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e110/100/90\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":null,"video":null},{"name":"Road Life","description":"While injured, not \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e and repairing a Generator:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you hit a basic great Skill Check, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you miss a basic Skill Check, you lose \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e token.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you have \u003cb\u003e6/5/4\u003c/b\u003e Tokens, spend all Tokens to heal \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% faster until you stop healing.","icon":null,"video":null}]},{"id":"vittoriotoscano","name":"Vittorio Toscano","bio":"Vittorio has endlessly wandered through the Fog, attempting to learn its secrets, for ages.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003ePotential Energy\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eFogwise\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eQuick Gambit\u003c/b\u003e allow him to store generator progress to use later, reveal the Killer\u0027s location after a great Skill Check, and give others a speed boost while repairing.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/39/S34_VittorioToscano_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Fogwise","description":"While repairing, whenever you hit a great basic Skill Check, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura for \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/90/IconPerks_fogwise.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Potential Energy","description":"While repairing, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to earn Tokens instead of progress, up to \u003cb\u003e10/15/20\u003c/b\u003e Tokens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile you have at least \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button2\u003c/b\u003e to spend all Tokens and gain \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e% progress for each Token spent.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you take damage, lose all Tokens.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/07/IconPerks_potentialEnergy.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2b/PotentialEnergy_Release.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Quick Gambit","description":"While chased by the Killer:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of other Survivors.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOther Survivors repair \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you take damage, cooldown: \u003cb\u003e40\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f7/IconPerks_quickGambit.png/revision/latest","video":null}]},{"id":"williambilloverbeck","name":"William \"Bill\" Overbeck","bio":"An old soldier, accustomed to dealing with critical situations.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eLeft Behind\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eBorrowed Time\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eUnbreakable\u003c/b\u003e, make him more powerful in dire moments.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/01/New_Store_Bill.png","perks":[{"name":"Borrowed Time","description":"Whenever you unhook a Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey retain their unhook \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003es longer.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey retain their unhook \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003es longer.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a3/IconPerks_borrowedTime.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/64/PerkAnimation_BorrowedTime.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Left Behind","description":"When all other Survivors are dead, while within \u003cb\u003e24/28/32\u003c/b\u003em of the Hatch, you see its Aura.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c3/IconPerks_leftBehind.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b5/PerkAnimation_LeftBehind.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Unbreakable","description":"Once per trial, while downed by the Killer, you can fully recover.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile downed, you recover \u003cb\u003e25/30/35\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4a/IconPerks_unbreakable.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/71/PerkAnimation_Unbreakable.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"yoichiasakawa","name":"Yoichi Asakawa","bio":"Yoichi is a brilliant marine biologist and psychic whose knowledge and abilities allow him to protect himself and assist others.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHis personal perks, \u003cb\u003eParental Guidance\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eEmpathic Connection\u003c/b\u003e, and \u003cb\u003eBoon: Dark Theory\u003c/b\u003e allow him to hide from Killers, call out to injured Survivors, and help others move faster.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/af/S30_YoichiAsakawa_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Boon: Dark Theory","description":"While next to a Totem, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to bless it, creating a unique Boon Totem that combines all your Boons.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors within the Boon\u0027s range gain \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e. When leaving the range, this ends after \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/60/IconPerks_boonDarkTheory.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/20/PerkAnimation_BoonDarkTheory.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Empathic Connection","description":"You heal other Survivors \u003cb\u003e25/30/35\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eInjured Survivors see your Aura.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/14/IconPerks_empathicConnection.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Parental Guidance","description":"Whenever you stun the Killer, for \u003cb\u003e5/6/7\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou make no Grunts of Pain.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/46/IconPerks_parentalGuidance.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b3/PerkAnimation_ParentalGuidance.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"yuikimura","name":"Yui Kimura","bio":"A hardened street racer, able to gain advantages for her and her fellow Survivors in challenging situations.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eLucky Break\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eAny Means Necessary\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eBreakout\u003c/b\u003e, enable her to cover her blood trails, reset dropped pallets, and assist helpless Survivors.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/13/S20_YuiKimura_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"Any Means Necessary","description":"While next to a Dropped Pallet, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e5/4/3\u003c/b\u003es to reset it.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou see the Auras of Dropped Pallets.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/79/IconPerks_anyMeansNecessary.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/86/PerkAnimation_AnyMeansNecessary.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Breakout","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003em of a carried Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e6/8/10\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe carried Survivor wiggles \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d0/IconPerks_breakout.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e9/PerkAnimation_Breakout.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Lucky Break","description":"While injured, for up to \u003cb\u003e40/50/60\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Pools of Blood.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou leave no Scratch Marks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each second spent healing another Survivor, recharge the duration by \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a7/IconPerks_luckyBreak.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/27/PerkAnimation_LuckyBreak.mp4/revision/latest"}]},{"id":"zarinakassir","name":"Zarina Kassir","bio":"A plucky documentarian, able to use her street smarts to avoid detection and greatly assist other Survivors.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer personal perks, \u003cb\u003eOff The Record\u003c/b\u003e, \u003cb\u003eRed Herring\u003c/b\u003e and \u003cb\u003eFor the People\u003c/b\u003e, help her remain hidden in the face of danger, create distractions, and quickly heal others by forgoing her own safety.","portrait":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d9/S21_ZarinaKassir_Portrait.png/revision/latest","perks":[{"name":"For the People","description":"While healthy and healing another Survivor without a Med-Kit, use \u003cb\u003eActivatable Button1\u003c/b\u003e to heal them instantly:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou take damage.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eBroken\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e80/70/60\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou become the Obsession.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the trial starts, you are less likely to be the Obsession.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/31/IconPerks_forThePeople.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5e/PerkAnimation_ForThePeople.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Off the Record","description":"Until all Generators are completed, whenever you are unhooked, for the next \u003cb\u003e30/35/40\u003c/b\u003es:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003eEndurance\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYour Grunts of Pain are \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% quieter.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Killer cannot see your Aura.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/9e/IconPerks_offTheRecord.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/83/PerkAnimation_OffTheRecord.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Red Herring","description":"After you repair a Generator for at least \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003es, you see its Aura.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen you hide in a Locker, the Killer is alerted to the Generator. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e25/20/15\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1c/IconPerks_redHerring.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/48/PerkAnimation_RedHerring_KillerPOV.mp4/revision/latest"}]}],"perks":{"survivor":[{"name":"Dark Sense","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, when the Killer gets within \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em of you, you see their Aura for \u003cb\u003e5/7/10\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/92/IconPerks_darkSense.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/07/PerkAnimation_DarkSense_FirstGen.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Deja Vu","description":"You see the Auras of the \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003e Generators closest to each other and repair them \u003cb\u003e4/5/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/89/IconPerks_dejaVu.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ed/PerkAnimation_DejaVu_Map.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Hope","description":"When all Generators are completed, you gain \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/18/IconPerks_hope.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/93/PerkAnimation_Hope.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Kindred","description":"While you are hooked, all Survivors see each others\u0027 Auras. While the Killer is within \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003em, all Survivors sees the Killer\u0027s Aura.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile another Survivor is hooked, you see the Auras of other Survivors. While the Killer is within \u003cb\u003e8/12/16\u003c/b\u003em of the hooked Survivor, you see the Killer\u0027s Aura.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a8/IconPerks_kindred.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ac/Kindred.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Lightweight","description":"Your Scratch Marks disappear \u003cb\u003e3/4/5\u003c/b\u003es faster and appear more spread out.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/67/IconPerks_lightweight.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ac/PerkAnimation_Lightweight.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"No One Left Behind","description":"When all Generators are completed:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou heal other Survivors \u003cb\u003e50/75/100\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unhook other Survivors \u003cb\u003e50/75/100\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWhenever you unhook a Survivor, they gain \u003cb\u003e10\u003c/b\u003e% more \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of other Survivors.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b0/IconPerks_noOneLeftBehind.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Plunderer\u0027s Instinct","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e32/48/64\u003c/b\u003em of locked Chests and dropped items, you see their Auras.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever you unlock a Chest, you are \u003cb\u003e50\u003c/b\u003e% more likely to find an item of higher rarity.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/28/IconPerks_plunderersInstinct.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ab/PerkAnimation_PlunderersInstinct.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Premonition","description":"While the Killer is within \u003cb\u003e36\u003c/b\u003em of you and inside a \u003cb\u003e45\u003c/b\u003e degree cone, whenever you look at them, you hear a sound cue. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e60/45/30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/39/IconPerks_premonition.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/df/PerkAnimation_Premonition.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Resilience","description":"While injured:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou bless and cleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou heal \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou open Exit Gates \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou repair \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou sabotage Hooks \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unhook Survivors \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unlock chests \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou vault \u003cb\u003e3/6/9\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/ee/IconPerks_resilience.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e2/PerkAnimation_Resilience_Chest.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Slippery Meat","description":"You can attempt to unhook yourself up to \u003cb\u003e6\u003c/b\u003e times and have \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e% more chance to succeed.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/03/IconPerks_slipperyMeat.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Small Game","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e8/10/12\u003c/b\u003em of you, whenever you look at a Totem in a \u003cb\u003e45\u003c/b\u003e degree cone, you hear a sound cue. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e14/12/10\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhenever a Survivor cleanses a Totem, you earn \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token, up to \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, the cone is \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003e degrees smaller.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/dc/IconPerks_smallGame.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/dd/PerkAnimation_SmallGame_Cleansing.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Spine Chill","description":"Within \u003cb\u003e36\u003c/b\u003em, whenever the Killer looks at you, you hear a sound cue.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e36\u003c/b\u003em, while the Killer is looking at you:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou bless and cleanse Totems \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou heal \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou open Exit Gates \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou repair Generators \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou sabotage Hooks \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unhook Survivors \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou unlock Chests \u003cb\u003e2/4/6\u003c/b\u003e% faster.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/57/IconPerks_spineChill.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/28/PerkAnimation_SpineChill_Cleansing.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"This Is Not Happening","description":"While injured, great basic Skill Check zones are \u003cb\u003e10/20/30\u003c/b\u003e% bigger.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/58/IconPerks_thisIsNotHappening.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/6b/PerkAnimation_ThisIsNotHappening.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"We\u0027ll make it","description":"Whenever you unhook a Survivor, for \u003cb\u003e30/60/90\u003c/b\u003es, you heal other Survivors \u003cb\u003e100\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8a/IconPerks_wellMakeIt.png/revision/latest","video":null}],"killer":[{"name":"Bitter Murmur","description":"Whenever a Generator is completed, you see the Auras of Survivors within \u003cb\u003e16\u003c/b\u003em of it for \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen all Generators are completed, you see the Auras of all Survivors for \u003cb\u003e5/7/10\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/IconPerks_bitterMurmur.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/56/PerkAnimation_BitterMurmur_LastGen.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Deerstalker","description":"Every \u003cb\u003e40/35/30\u003c/b\u003es, the Survivor with the least time in chase sees your Aura for \u003cb\u003e3\u003c/b\u003es.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile a Survivor sees your Aura, you see their Aura.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/01/IconPerks_deerstalker.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/71/Deerstalker.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Distressing","description":"Your Terror Radius is \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% larger.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/94/IconPerks_distressing.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: No One Escapes Death","description":"When all Generators are completed, a Dull Totem ignites:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eSurvivors gain \u003cb\u003eExposed\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou gain \u003cb\u003e2/3/4\u003c/b\u003e% \u003cb\u003eHaste\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWithin \u003cb\u003e4\u003c/b\u003em, Survivors see the Hex Totem\u0027s Aura, expanding to \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em over \u003cb\u003e30\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/af/IconPerks_hexNoOneEscapesDeath.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Hex: Thrill of the Hunt","description":"When the trial starts, a Dull Totem ignites.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Dull and Hex Totem remaining, you have \u003cb\u003e1\u003c/b\u003e Token.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFor each Token, Survivors bless and cleanse totems \u003cb\u003e8/9/10\u003c/b\u003e% slower.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/02/IconPerks_hexThrillOfTheHunt.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Insidious","description":"After being idle for \u003cb\u003e3/2/1\u003c/b\u003es, you gain \u003cb\u003eUndetectable\u003c/b\u003e until you act.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/40/IconPerks_insidious.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/ff/Insidious_SurvivorPOV.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Iron Grasp","description":"While carrying a Survivor:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey wiggle \u003cb\u003e4/8/12\u003c/b\u003e% slower.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eTheir wiggle is \u003cb\u003e75\u003c/b\u003e% weaker.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/14/IconPerks_ironGrasp.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Scourge Hook: Monstrous Shrine","description":"When the trial starts:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e4 random Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe Basement Hooks become Scourge Hooks.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhile you are at least \u003cb\u003e24\u003c/b\u003em away from a Survivor on a Scourge Hook, they are sacrificed \u003cb\u003e10/15/20\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/91/IconPerks_scourgeHookMonstrousShrine.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Shattered Hope","description":"Whenever you snuff a Boon Totem:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eYou see the Auras of all Survivors within its range for \u003cb\u003e6/7/8\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIt is destroyed.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/aa/IconPerks_shatteredHope.png/revision/latest","video":null},{"name":"Sloppy Butcher","description":"Whenever you damage a Survivor with a basic-attack:\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eHemorrhage\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e70/80/90\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThey gain \u003cb\u003eMangled\u003c/b\u003e for \u003cb\u003e70/80/90\u003c/b\u003es.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSurvivors with \u003cb\u003eHemorrhage\u003c/b\u003e lose healing progress \u003cb\u003e25\u003c/b\u003e% faster.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/IconPerks_sloppyButcher.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/07/SloppyButcher.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Spies from the Shadows","description":"Whenever a Survivor scares a Crow within \u003cb\u003e20/28/36\u003c/b\u003em of you, you are alerted. Cooldown: \u003cb\u003e5\u003c/b\u003es.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b1/IconPerks_spiesFromTheShadows.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/81/SpiesfromtheShadows.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Unrelenting","description":"Whenever you miss a basic-attack, your cooldown is \u003cb\u003e20/25/30\u003c/b\u003e% shorter.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/57/IconPerks_unrelenting.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/db/Unrelenting.mp4/revision/latest"},{"name":"Whispers","description":"While within \u003cb\u003e48/40/32\u003c/b\u003em of a Survivor, you randomly hear whispers.","icon":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/bb/IconPerks_whispers.png/revision/latest","video":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f4/Whispers.mp4/revision/latest"}]},"maps":[{"id":"azarovsrestingplace","name":"Azarov’s Resting Place","realm":"Autohaven Wreckers","description":"The Office is where money changed owners and hands were shook. The heavy duty safe in the floor might have been a dead giveaway to the shady business that took place. Wads of cash were hidden all over the place. Stating that money wasn’t an issue, maybe people got executed for enjoyment, rather than wealth.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/57/IconMap_Jnk_Office.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"bloodlodge","name":"Blood Lodge","realm":"Autohaven Wreckers","description":"A run-down log cabin at the edge of the scrap yard and the home of its owner. Weird carvings and etchings in the wall perhaps say more about the owner’s state of mind and allude to his disappearance. Reports suggested that prisoners were held in its dark basement before they were taken to the crusher.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/IconMap_Jnk_Lodge.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7a/AltMapOutline_Jnk_Lodge.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"gasheaven","name":"Gas Heaven","realm":"Autohaven Wreckers","description":"For decades, Azarov’s Gas Heaven offered the last chance for travellers to rest and fuel up before the long, hard haul through the backcountry. Wiser travellers learned to decline that offer. The phones never worked and people had a peculiar habit of going missing. When the highway came through, bypassing Gas Heaven entirely, business dried up and the gas station was abandoned. No one quite knows how many bodies are stashed out there, or what else is hidden in the ruins of the old rest stop.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d2/IconMap_Jnk_GasStation.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/26/AltMapOutline_Jnk_GasStation.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"wreckersyard","name":"Wreckers\u0027 Yard","realm":"Autohaven Wreckers","description":"The Junkyard is packed with sharp objects. Walking around the area, aware of the bloodbath that took place here, changes the landscape. Blood-covered metal and bits of flesh abound. One does not willingly walk amongst all this evidence of death.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/3d/IconMap_Jnk_Scrapyard.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c5/AltMapOutline_Jnk_Scrapyard.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"wretchedshop","name":"Wretched Shop","realm":"Autohaven Wreckers","description":"This old garage was once not just a place of death and execution. Automobiles were actually repaired here amongst oil mixed with blood. But as investigators found out about the atrocities that took place, it became forgotten.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4d/IconMap_Jnk_Garage.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"grimpantry","name":"Grim Pantry","realm":"Backwater Swamp","description":"One shack stood apart from the rest of the village. Once the water was drained and the area beneath the base was revealed, the true horror of the swamp\u0027s cage was discovered. It was here that the prisoners, if that\u0027s what we should call them, were brought. Held in the water, their bodies bloating horrendously, they were plucked, one by one for the family\u0027s needs. The stilts that kept the building upright acted as the only bars that awful jail needed.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d0/IconMap_Swp_GrimPantry.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"thepalerose","name":"The Pale Rose","realm":"Backwater Swamp","description":"The Pale Rose, an ancient paddle steamer in the middle of the swamp, is held captive by the stagnant mud. It has been here long before the residents began their hunt, a barely visible silhouette from the nearby village. There are signs of inhabitation, particularly in the upper states room where strange, ritualistic markings in dried blood and dirt cover the floor. From the scale of the bloodletting, something horrid has taken place here.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c1/IconMap_Swp_ThePaleRose.png","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f9/AltMapOutline_Swp_PaleRose.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"fracturedcowshed","name":"Fractured Cowshed","realm":"Coldwind Farm","description":"The old run-down cowshed was one of the first barns the Thompsons built on Coldwind Farm. It was originally intended to house sick animals at a safe distance from the rest of the livestock, but no animal who entered it ever survived. An investigation revealed the building was infested with toxic mold. The Thompsons figured it must be a construction fault or something to do with the dampness of the wood. A new barn was built, and the old cowshed was left to rot in the shadows.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/32/IconMap_Frm_Barn.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/74/AltMapOutline_Frm_Barn.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"rancidabattoir","name":"Rancid Abattoir","realm":"Coldwind Farm","description":"Once part of the farm, the slaughterhouse was still in operation for many years after the breakup of the farmland. Rotting stench and stained floors provide proof of all the deaths that have taken place here… animal or otherwise.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/94/IconMap_Frm_Slaughterhouse.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/4b/AltMapOutline_Frm_Slaughterhouse.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"rottenfields","name":"Rotten Fields","realm":"Coldwind Farm","description":"Even before the fall of Coldwind Farm, the cornfields were surrounded by tales of ominous myths. Everything from mutilated animals to red corn stalks. Now it’s abandoned, but still, someone seems to care for the corn in some way as the stalks still stand tall.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cd/IconMap_Frm_Cornfield.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/3/33/AltMapOutline_Frm_Cornfield.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"thethompsonhouse","name":"The Thompson House","realm":"Coldwind Farm","description":"The centerpiece of Coldwind Farm, the farmhouse stood proudly over the fields of golden corn for decades. After the horrific events of 1972, the building fell into disrepair and eventual ruin. The farmhouse is now nothing more than a forgotten, former home where holidays were once celebrated.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/62/IconMap_Frm_Farmhouse.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/65/AltMapOutline_Frm_Farmhouse.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"tormentcreek","name":"Torment Creek","realm":"Coldwind Farm","description":"The Silo is one of the oldest remaining buildings that made up Coldwind Farm. The great storm of 2003 brought the ancient structure crashing down. It was weeks later that searchers discovered twelve bodies were buried in the ruins. Their crushed corpses were buried deep in the slurry that oozed out from the base and made identification almost impossible.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a3/IconMap_Frm_Silo.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"disturbedward","name":"Disturbed Ward","realm":"Crotus Prenn Asylum","description":"The last standing structure after the fire that still shows the grandeur of the original architecture. Its two floors and dark basement leave behind nothing of the tale of horrors that took place here. Nothing but memories linger in the abandoned rooms.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/77/IconMap_Asy_Asylum.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/7e/AltMapOutline_Asy_Asylum.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"fathercampbellschapel","name":"Father Campbell\u0027s Chapel","realm":"Crotus Prenn Asylum","description":"Nestled in a quiet part of the grounds, Father Campbell’s Chapel was a haven from the horrors of the rest of the asylum. Those patients whose illnesses were less severe were given the run of the place and many would come here for refuge, to communicate with God and confess their sins.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSadly, Father Campbell’s legacy of good works counted for nothing when the Nurse’s mind snapped, and he drew his final breath in the confessional that had helped so many.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNow the chapel has been joined by a strange companion: a carny’s caravan, pulled by a shadowy horse. It has long traveled through The Fog, moving from realm to realm, and now temporarily camps here.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBeware: only a fool would let the bright colors seduce them into visiting.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/87/IconMap_Asy_Chapel.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/04/AltMapOutline_Asy_Chapel.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"nostromowreckage","name":"Nostromo Wreckage","realm":"Dvarka Deepwood","description":"A brutal, industrial interstellar cargo ship, where human life takes a back seat to cruel efficiency. Death lurks around every corner of its labyrinthine decks. From the well of Ripley’s memories a grim and hopeless realm manifests into a terrifying nightmare.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/42/IconMap_Uba_Wormholelevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"tobalanding","name":"Toba Landing","realm":"Dvarka Deepwood","description":"After years hurtling through the inky blackness of deep space, a solitary colony ship descended to the surface of Dvarka. Selected for its breathable air, its valuable minerals, and its beautiful lakes and forests, Dvarka looked to be the perfect planet for a new start for humanity. But exploration of the surface revealed a dark secret: an advanced civilization, completely wiped out by some unknown event.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe ship lies surrounded by strange rock formations on the alien soil of Dvarka, the light of its sun choked out by giant, twisting trees. And in the darkness, a new threat emerges: an Earth invention, twisted by alien technology, unflagging in its mission to end human life on Dvarka and beyond.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/4/40/IconMap_Uba_Umbralevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"deadsands","name":"Dead Sands","realm":"Forsaken Boneyard","description":"Taken on the verge of death, Carmina Mora will never escape the desert where her friends were murdered.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Entity’s Realm is an ever-changing mockery of those who dwell within it, and the land where she lost her hands and tongue exists in flux. The cursed crows will find no sanctuary here, and even the simplest source of refuge may hold dangers of its own. Only the stone sentinels looming overhead remain, gazing down beneath their shrouds, bound to witness the endless cycle of bloodshed.","image":null,"layouts":[]},{"id":"eyrieofcrows","name":"Eyrie of Crows","realm":"Forsaken Boneyard","description":"In the dust-choked expanse of the Chilean desert lies a graveyard abandoned by the living, battered by the passage of time. Only through violence was it once more given prominence, hosting the gruesome murder of the artist Carmina Mora and her friends.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWithin The Entity\u0027s realm, the humble lot has been twisted into a grand celebration of the bloody events that took place. A towering crypt offers a roost for the crows to observe the trial, beady eyes gazing with fascination, never forgetting the day they fed greedily on the flesh of screaming men and women.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fb/IconMap_Ion_Ionlevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"thegame","name":"The Game","realm":"Gideon Meat Plant","description":"This industrial warehouse is the product of a fevered mind, desperately trying to complete their life’s work, their legacy, before their inevitable end. A place of both, creation and destruction, from which devices of death and rebirth were produced. The smell of fear, blood and death has soaked into the brick walls. The sickly glow of fluorescent lighting bathes the room where Jigsaw has planned out his final trial.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe game begins.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/58/IconMap_Fin_TheGame.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/2/2a/AltMapOutline_Fin_Hideout_down.png/revision/latest","https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0b/AltMapOutline_Fin_Hideout_up.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"deaddawgsaloon","name":"Dead Dawg Saloon","realm":"Grave of Glenvale","description":"An early settlement on the unforgiving frontier, the outpost of Glenvale was snuffed out in a ruthless, bloody gang war. Responding to the abduction of five brothers-in-arms, the Hellshire Gang stormed in with six-shooters and dynamite. What began as a standoff with the Mason Kelly Gang quickly broke down into a chaotic war zone. Guns fired indiscriminately in a desperate bid for self-preservation, cutting through gang members and civilians alike.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWhen the dust settled, the dead outnumbered the living. The hostages were discovered to have been long killed, their bodies disemboweled, guts strewn across town. In a silent rage, the few surviving Hellshire members rounded up their injured enemies and finished them in the same gruesome manner. By nightfall, only the crows remained, feasting gluttonously upon their victory.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/8e/IconMap_Ukr_Saloon.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/1e/AltMapOutline_Ukr_Saloon.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"lampkinlane","name":"Lampkin Lane","realm":"Haddonfield","description":"A simple street with houses that witnessed the horrors that took place. A jungle gym where children once learned to climb. Sidewalks where fathers taught their daughters to ride a bike. All gone. Instead it sits in the palm of The Entity, forever held in darkness.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/07/IconMap_Sub_Street.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b7/AltMapOutline_Sub_Street.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"theundergroundcomplex","name":"The Underground Complex","realm":"Hawkins National Laboratory","description":"Located below the Hawkins National Laboratory, this underground complex released dozens of interdimensional creatures in November 1984, before the rift was sealed.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe site kept some vestiges of its past as the mental health institute, including a moldy isolation tank used by patients suffering from acute anxiety that was later modernized for mind control experimentation on promising test subjects.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNow the walls of the abandoned facility are sprayed with bullets and blood, evidence of a battle against interdimensional creatures.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/ab/IconMap_Qat_Laboratory.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"treatmenttheater","name":"Treatment Theater","realm":"Léry\u0027s Memorial Institute","description":"A mansion from the late 1800\u0027s - donated and transformed into a medical facility and later into a CIA black site specializing in cutting-edge interrogation techniques. The institute closing is shrouded in controversy and mystery. At the heart of the facility, the Doctor’s tools have been arranged in a twisted ritual circle, ready for research, as he refines his methods on an endless stream of terrified patients.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/15/IconMap_Hos_Treatment.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a0/AltMapOutline_Hos_Treatment.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"mountormondresort","name":"Mount Ormond Resort","realm":"Ormond","description":"Ormond was once a small, remote ski town with idyllic slopes, but its resort turned obsolete when a deluxe ski village was built on Mount Richards less than two hours away. Mount Richards offered fresh slopes with luxurious stores and hotels, which crushed Mount Ormond’s isolated, decrepit facilities.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe fate of the mountain worsened when a mining project took interest in the coal present at its summit. The mountaintop was lined by explosives to extract coal seams from under it. The project caused a public outrage and was stopped midway.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eMount Ormond is now a soulful, deforested graveyard where gangs and teenagers go looking for trouble. Some people say that the mountain hides a darkness, a bottomless hole from where no one can return.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d4/IconMap_Kny_Cottage.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/70/AltMapOutline_Kny_Cottage.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"ormondlakemine","name":"Ormond Lake Mine","realm":"Ormond","description":"Tucked among the majestic slopes near Ormond there lies a deep scar running through the rock and roots. The promise of its vast natural resources drew unscrupulous surveyors to its ice-capped peaks. Upon discovering rich coal deposits, they set up shop, but a series of unexplainable mishaps forced them to close the mine before it was exhausted.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThey abandoned the complex and left the nearby town to pick up the pieces. After laying silent for decades, rumors swirl that someone else has taken residence among the rusting machines... a group whose motivations are far darker, and far more mysterious.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAt night, an uneasy silence falls over the complex, punctuated only by the groaning of decaying machines.","image":null,"layouts":[]},{"id":"raccooncitypolicestationeastwing","name":"Raccoon City Police Station East Wing","realm":"Raccoon City","description":"The smell of blood and festering limbs permeated the concrete walls of the Raccoon City police station. Once an art museum, the building was converted into a precinct at the heart of the city. But when evil took residence, the station showed one last terrifying exhibition: corpses crowding narrow corridors, blood smeared on shattered windows, and festering flesh dripping down the stairs.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/6/68/IconMap_Ecl_Eclipselevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"raccooncitypolicestationwestwing","name":"Raccoon City Police Station West Wing","realm":"Raccoon City","description":"The smell of blood and festering limbs permeated the concrete walls of the Raccoon City police station. Once an art museum, the building was converted into a precinct at the heart of the city. But when evil took residence, the station showed one last terrifying exhibition: corpses crowding narrow corridors, blood smeared on shattered windows, and festering flesh dripping down the stairs.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/fa/IconMap_Ecl_Orionlevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"mothersdwelling","name":"Mother\u0027s Dwelling","realm":"Red Forest","description":"Deep in a forest with many names lies a hidden home. The family that once lived there was dependent on the forest… and was broken by it. More than a century old, the dwelling is in surprisingly good condition, though it shows signs of often being patched and mended. The forest holds the house tightly in its grasp, growing over and around it like a second skin. Only once inside is it clear that someone still lives there. It is warm and welcoming and lovingly decorated, with a large living space, a bedroom and a corner dedicated for little ones. Here they are protected from the harsh winter of the northern forest.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/01/IconMap_Brl_MadHouse.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"thetempleofpurgation","name":"The Temple of Purgation","realm":"Red Forest","description":"The half-forgotten temple complex dedicated to the cleansing of the High Priestess’s followers. The vertiginous hypostyle hall was believed to hold the weight of the heavens.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eStolen from the memories of The Plague, the temple was planted in the howling Red Forest, whose winds eroded its smooth edges. It now stands as a beacon of fear, visible from all cardinal points.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d4/IconMap_Brl_Temple.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"midwichelementaryschool","name":"Midwich Elementary School","realm":"Silent Hill","description":"To students who were bullied by their teachers and classmates, attending Midwich Elementary School was comparable to torture. As the Order’s grip on the town’s supernatural energies tightened, a transformation occurred. The childhood trauma that took place in the building manifested itself into a twisted, nightmarish design.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThough desks and textbooks remain, they’re eerily contrasted with stained walls, rusted chains, and hanging cadavers. Any notion that this could have been a place of innocence and learning has long since faded.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d5/IconMap_Wal_Level01.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"trickstersdelusion","name":"Trickster\u0027s Delusion","realm":"Sleepless District","description":"Hak Ji-woon had spent years refining his sound, his image, his style. In one fell swoop, all of it was taken from him and put on a virtual idol.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHe walked the neon neighborhood in a rage. Even the signs seemed to predict the end of his career. Violent imaginings flooded his mind. If only he could kill everyone in and around that club, consequences be damned. But no. Vengeance would be reserved for those who brought MiNA to life.","image":null,"layouts":[]},{"id":"badhampreschooli","name":"Badham Preschool I","realm":"Springwood","description":"This is not the Badham Preschool where children laughed and learned, made lifelong friendships and had their paintings hung on the walls. This is a dark echo created from the nightmares of those who suffered there. The walls creak under the burden of history. Events that should be long forgotten are recorded forever in the plaster and stone, pervading the building with misery. Only one part of the building is accurately reflected in this darkness. The squalid room where Freddy Krueger lived and worked. The hidden basement area where he committed the heinous acts that appalled a town and condemned him to death. This is a place of the subconscious, of the nightmare brought into hideous reality.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cf/IconMap_Eng_Elmstreet.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"badhampreschoolii","name":"Badham Preschool II","realm":"Springwood","description":"This is not the Badham Preschool where children laughed and learned, made lifelong friendships and had their paintings hung on the walls. This is a dark echo created from the nightmares of those who suffered there. The walls creak under the burden of history. Events that should be long forgotten are recorded forever in the plaster and stone, pervading the building with misery. Only one part of the building is accurately reflected in this darkness. The squalid room where Freddy Krueger lived and worked. The hidden basement area where he committed the heinous acts that appalled a town and condemned him to death. This is a place of the subconscious, of the nightmare brought into hideous reality.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cf/IconMap_Eng_Elmstreet.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"badhampreschooliii","name":"Badham Preschool III","realm":"Springwood","description":"This is not the Badham Preschool where children laughed and learned, made lifelong friendships and had their paintings hung on the walls. This is a dark echo created from the nightmares of those who suffered there. The walls creak under the burden of history. Events that should be long forgotten are recorded forever in the plaster and stone, pervading the building with misery. Only one part of the building is accurately reflected in this darkness. The squalid room where Freddy Krueger lived and worked. The hidden basement area where he committed the heinous acts that appalled a town and condemned him to death. This is a place of the subconscious, of the nightmare brought into hideous reality.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cf/IconMap_Eng_Elmstreet.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"badhampreschooliv","name":"Badham Preschool IV","realm":"Springwood","description":"This is not the Badham Preschool where children laughed and learned, made lifelong friendships and had their paintings hung on the walls. This is a dark echo created from the nightmares of those who suffered there. The walls creak under the burden of history. Events that should be long forgotten are recorded forever in the plaster and stone, pervading the building with misery. Only one part of the building is accurately reflected in this darkness. The squalid room where Freddy Krueger lived and worked. The hidden basement area where he committed the heinous acts that appalled a town and condemned him to death. This is a place of the subconscious, of the nightmare brought into hideous reality.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cf/IconMap_Eng_Elmstreet.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"badhampreschoolv","name":"Badham Preschool V","realm":"Springwood","description":"This is not the Badham Preschool where children laughed and learned, made lifelong friendships and had their paintings hung on the walls. This is a dark echo created from the nightmares of those who suffered there. The walls creak under the burden of history. Events that should be long forgotten are recorded forever in the plaster and stone, pervading the building with misery. Only one part of the building is accurately reflected in this darkness. The squalid room where Freddy Krueger lived and worked. The hidden basement area where he committed the heinous acts that appalled a town and condemned him to death. This is a place of the subconscious, of the nightmare brought into hideous reality.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/cf/IconMap_Eng_Elmstreet.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"forgottenruins","name":"Forgotten Ruins","realm":"The Decimated Borgo","description":"Pulled from the memories of alchemists, warriors, storytellers, and criminals, the Forgotten Ruins is an amalgamation of hidden knowledge and dark secrets.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHow many have wandered this dead terrain, unaware of what lurked beneath their feet? And how many more ventured down to the bottom of that decaying staircase, only to succumb to what awaited them","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/9/91/IconMap_Qtm_Churroslevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"theshatteredsquare","name":"The Shattered Square","realm":"The Decimated Borgo","description":"Daro, a village that once bustled with life and industry, suddenly razed to the ground. The gorgeous, cobbled roads of this medieval Italian settlement ran red with the blood of her citizens, all due to the “righteousness” of the Guardia Compagnia.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Entity’s Realm has preserved and distorted this ancient village, its rubble forever smoldering. A large gathering hall stands in its center, still upright despite its scars. Several shacks litter the landscape in varying degrees of disrepair. The pain suffered here still emanates from the crackles of its embers.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/e/e3/IconMap_Qtm_Quantumlevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"coaltower","name":"Coal Tower","realm":"The MacMillan Estate","description":"Once used for storing the coal that fueled the Foundry, it now lies abandoned. The roof is split wide open, suggesting some titanic explosion, but the angles don’t seem to make sense. So to fathom its destiny is not done easily - even if one would want to.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/f/f6/IconMap_Ind_CoalTower.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/8/85/AltMapOutline_Ind_CoalTower.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"groaningstorehouse","name":"Groaning Storehouse","realm":"The MacMillan Estate","description":"On the eastern edge of the estate, near the woods, lie the remains of the MacMillan warehouse. Dwarfing the surrounding buildings, the massive storehouse can often be heard creaking and groaning as if it were crying out with the anguish of the incinerated laborers.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/c/c9/IconMap_Ind_Storehouse.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"ironworksofmisery","name":"Ironworks of Misery","realm":"The MacMillan Estate","description":"The beating heart of the Mine, the Foundry was where the iron ore was directly smelted into vast ingots. The huge vats still bear evidence of the bodies that were incinerated within them - preserved in the metal residue.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/de/IconMap_Ind_Foundry.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b1/AltMapOutline_Ind_Foundry.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"shelterwoods","name":"Shelter Woods","realm":"The MacMillan Estate","description":"A makeshift command center was erected here, its rigid walls and sharp angles standing in stark contrast to the twisted wood and soil. For those who chance upon this crude structure, the realization that this complex belongs to an apex hunter—a hunter whose prey is human—usually comes too late.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/d/d8/IconMap_Ind_Forest.png/revision/latest","layouts":[]},{"id":"suffocationpit","name":"Suffocation Pit","realm":"The MacMillan Estate","description":"You can still see the tiny entrance that miners used to haul the ore to the surface. Now it is nothing more than a pile of rubble. No one bothered to clear it as they feared whatever might be found inside. Instead it fell into oblivion.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/IconMap_Ind_Mine.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0f/AltMapOutline_Ind_Mine.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"fallenrefuge","name":"Fallen Refuge","realm":"Withered Isle","description":"Amid the overgrown grass, a new structure rose from the darkness. Twisted and contorted as if from a dream, melding the architecture of a prison tower—an erstwhile safe haven for the survivors of an apocalyptic outbreak—and a hospital that once healed the people of King County.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIts cruel form stretches into the night sky, a mockery of what these structures represented. Symbols of security and compassion, corrupted into cruel reminders that those in the Entity\u0027s realm are always watched… and can never leave.","image":null,"layouts":[]},{"id":"freddyfazbearspizza","name":"Freddy Fazbear\u0027s Pizza","realm":"Withered Isle","description":"The rotting brainchild of a sadistic murderer still stands over the grassy plains. A place of joy for some, and unspeakable terror for others. Do not let the bright colors and parlor tricks deceive you; many have died within these walls, and many more will die still.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/7/72/IconMap_Meteor_Applepielevel02.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"gardenofjoy","name":"Garden of Joy","realm":"Withered Isle","description":"On a privately-owned island in the Atlantic, the Garden was home to a bustling commune of optimists set on building a better world. Funded by a band of anonymous philanthropists and managed by a charismatic leader, they attempted to rid themselves of dark emotions, for fear of summoning the ancient god of shadows.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eDark thoughts corrupted this idyllic community. A mansion sits twisted by darkness and further perverted by the Entity’s influence, contorting and reconfiguring itself in maddening, serpentine formations. At once familiar and foreign, to look upon it is to know fear.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/a/a7/IconMap_Meteor_Meteorlevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"greenvillesquare","name":"Greenville Square","realm":"Withered Isle","description":"A thin slice of small-town Americana, long abandoned, long forgotten.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGreenville was always meant to be a place for those who felt like they didn’t belong, a town founded by pilgrims fleeing persecution. Those pilgrims still watch over the environment, their fierce determination lovingly portrayed in a statue that stands tall in the center of town.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNow in the Entity’s Realm, something wanders freely along the overgrown streets: a writhing creature responsible for a string of disappearances across the country going back decades. Even the local cinema, a hub of fantasy and escapism, provides no sanctuary from the evil that will never die.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/0/0f/IconMap_Meteor_Applepielevel01.png","layouts":[]},{"id":"familyresidence","name":"Family Residence","realm":"Yamaoka Estate","description":"While the Yamaoka estate displayed a glorious past, but the family residence was falling apart. The house needed numerous renovations to remain habitable.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe last generation of the Yamaoka family were facing troubled times. Their finances were dire and the situation worsened when the daughter started university, just a few months before the mother became ill. Shouldering both university fees and hospital bills, the father worked past exhaustion.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eTo keep a roof over their heads, he profaned their legacy. The walls of their ancestral home were sealed with moldy materials for a cheap fix.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAs the house was stripped of its integrity, an old anger was awakened.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/5a/IconMap_Hti_Manor.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/1/19/AltMapOutline_Hti_Manor.png/revision/latest"]},{"id":"sanctumofwrath","name":"Sanctum of Wrath","realm":"Yamaoka Estate","description":"Once opulent and well-tended by priests, the shrine was abandoned for reasons unknown. Season after season, the harsh and unforgiving weather corroded its grandeur. Paths that welcomed weary travelers, were now thick with vegetation growing damp and unrestrained. The sculptures were a haven for moss and lichen, concealing a scratched and brittle stone.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eKazan shuddered with rage as he stepped into the area. Unable to restrain himself, he unleashed his might on a statue atop the shrine, clubbing its arms and head to pieces. Even after he left, a rot seemed to pervade the air. The chimes of bells played softly on the wind, as everything around them crumbled. Torn from Kazan\u0027s memories, the shrine now stood on the estate of his childhood home—a trick by The Entity that infuriated him even more.","image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/b/b8/IconMap_Hti_Shrine.png/revision/latest","layouts":["https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/deadbydaylight_gamepedia_en/images/5/51/AltMapOutline_Hti_Shrine.png/revision/latest"]}]};
